INSERT INTO `bns_sections` VALUES (1,'BNS 100','Murder','IPC 302','Offences Against Human Body','Culpable homicide is \"murder\" if the act is done with the intention of causing death, or with intention of causing such bodily injury as the offender knows to be likely to cause death, or with intention of causing bodily injury sufficient in ordinary course of nature to cause death. BNS 100 defines the circumstances that elevate culpable homicide to murder - the gravest offence against the human body in Indian law.','Death penalty or Imprisonment for Life + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(2,'BNS 101','Culpable Homicide not amounting to Murder','IPC 304','Offences Against Human Body','Culpable homicide is the act of causing death with the intention of causing death or bodily injury likely to cause death, or with the knowledge that the act is likely to cause death - but does not meet the higher threshold of murder. This section creates a graduated scale between accidental death and premeditated murder, allowing courts to distinguish the degree of criminal intent.','Imprisonment up to 10 years or Life + Fine (based on intent)',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(3,'BNS 102','Punishment for Murder by Life Convict','IPC 303','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever, being under sentence of imprisonment for life, commits murder shall be punished with death. This section specifically targets those who are already serving a life sentence when they commit another murder, treating the re-offence as the most extreme case warranting capital punishment.','Death penalty (mandatory)',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(4,'BNS 105','Culpable Homicide by Negligence','IPC 304A','Offences Against Human Body','Causing the death of any person by a rash or negligent act which does not amount to culpable homicide. This section typically applies to road accident fatalities caused by reckless driving, medical negligence resulting in death, or industrial accidents caused by gross disregard for safety norms.','Imprisonment up to 5 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(5,'BNS 80','Dowry Death','IPC 304B','Offences Against Women','Where the death of a woman is caused by burns or bodily injury or occurs under suspicious circumstances within 7 years of marriage, and it is shown that she was subjected to cruelty or harassment by her husband or his relatives in connection with demand of dowry - such death is called \"dowry death\". The husband and relatives are deemed to have caused her death.','Imprisonment for not less than 7 years, extendable to Life',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(6,'BNS 108','Abetment of Suicide','IPC 306','Offences Against Human Body','If any person commits suicide, whoever abets the commission of such suicide shall be punished. Abetment here includes instigation, conspiracy, and intentional aiding. This section is frequently invoked in cases of harassment leading to suicide, such as workplace bullying, mental torture by family members, and online harassment.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(7,'BNS 109','Attempt to Murder','IPC 307','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever does any act with such intention or knowledge, and under such circumstances, that if by that act he caused death, he would be guilty of murder - and if hurt is caused to any person by such act - shall be punished. Even if no injury results, the attempt itself is punishable. The critical element is the intent to cause death.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine; if victim is hurt, Life Imprisonment',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(8,'BNS 115','Voluntarily Causing Hurt','IPC 323','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever voluntarily causes hurt to any person shall be punished. \"Hurt\" means the causing of bodily pain, disease, or infirmity to any person. This is a baseline offence covering all forms of physical assault that do not rise to the level of grievous hurt. It forms the foundation of most assault-related criminal proceedings.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(9,'BNS 117','Voluntarily Causing Grievous Hurt','IPC 325','Offences Against Human Body','\"Grievous hurt\" includes emasculation, permanent loss of sight or hearing, privation of any member or joint, destruction of any member or joint, permanent disfiguration of the head or face, fracture or dislocation of a bone or tooth, and any hurt that endangers life or causes severe bodily pain for 20 days or more. This section punishes intentional infliction of such serious injuries.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(10,'BNS 124','Voluntarily Throwing or Administering Acid','IPC 326A','Offences Against Women','Whoever throws or attempts to throw acid, or administers acid or attempts to administer acid, on any person with the intention of causing permanent or partial damage or deformity or burns or maiming or disfigurement or disability or grievous hurt - shall be punished. Acid attacks cause irreversible trauma and this section provides stringent punishment reflecting societal condemnation.','Imprisonment of not less than 10 years, extendable to Life + Fine (paid to victim)',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(11,'BNS 126','Wrongful Restraint','IPC 339','Offences Against Liberty','Whoever voluntarily obstructs any person so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction in which that person has a right to proceed is said to wrongfully restrain that person. This is a foundational liberty offence - even a temporary physical obstruction of a person\'s movement without legal authority constitutes wrongful restraint.','Imprisonment up to 1 month, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(12,'BNS 127','Wrongful Confinement','IPC 340','Offences Against Liberty','Whoever wrongfully restrains any person in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits is said to wrongfully confine that person. Unlike wrongful restraint (which blocks a path), wrongful confinement encircles the person entirely - creating a perimeter they cannot cross without physical force.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(13,'BNS 132','Assault','IPC 351','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever makes any gesture or preparation intending or knowing it to be likely that such gesture or preparation will cause any person present to apprehend that the person making the gesture is about to use criminal force on that person is said to commit an assault. Note: words alone cannot constitute an assault, but words accompanied by gestures can.','Imprisonment up to 3 months, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(14,'BNS 63','Rape','IPC 375','Offences Against Women','A man is said to commit \"rape\" who has sexual intercourse with a woman under circumstances falling under 7 specified descriptions - including against her will, without her consent, by fraudulently obtaining consent, when she is unable to consent due to intoxication, or when she is under 18 years of age. Consent given under fear of death or hurt does not constitute valid consent.','Rigorous Imprisonment not less than 10 years, extendable to Life + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(15,'BNS 69','Sexual Intercourse by Deceitful Means','IPC 493/376','Offences Against Women','Whoever, by deceitful means or by making promise to marry a woman without any intention of fulfilling the promise, has sexual intercourse with her, such sexual intercourse not amounting to rape, shall be punished. This section specifically addresses betrayal of trust through false promises of marriage.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(16,'BNS 74','Assault or Criminal Force on Woman with Intent to Outrage Modesty','IPC 354','Offences Against Women','Whoever assaults or uses criminal force on any woman, intending to outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage her modesty, shall be punished. This section protects the dignity and modesty of women in public and private spaces alike and covers a wide range of non-consensual physical contact.','Imprisonment of not less than 1 year, extendable to 5 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(17,'BNS 79','Obscene Acts or Words to Insult Modesty of Woman','IPC 509','Offences Against Women','Whoever, intending to insult the modesty of any woman, utters any word, makes any sound or gesture, or exhibits any object, intending that such word or sound shall be heard, or that such gesture or object shall be seen, by such woman - or intrudes upon the privacy of such woman - shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(18,'BNS 303','Theft','IPC 378','Offences Against Property','Whoever, intending to take dishonestly any moveable property out of the possession of any person without that person\'s consent, moves that property in order to take it, is said to commit theft. \"Dishonest intention\" is the key element - even momentary taking with dishonest intent constitutes theft. Immoveable property, however, cannot be \"stolen\" under this section.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(19,'BNS 304','Punishment for Theft','IPC 379','Offences Against Property','Theft being proved, the accused shall be punished under this section unless a special section applies (e.g., theft from a dwelling or vehicle). It provides the baseline punishment for the offence of theft defined in BNS 303, creating a consistent sentencing framework for property offences.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(20,'BNS 308','Extortion','IPC 383','Offences Against Property','Whoever intentionally puts any person in fear of any injury to that person or to any other person, and thereby dishonestly induces the person so put in fear to deliver to any person any property or valuable security, or to do or refrain from doing anything which may result in loss or damage to that person, commits \"extortion\". The fear is the tool - property is the goal.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(21,'BNS 310','Robbery','IPC 390','Offences Against Property','In all robbery there is either theft or extortion. Theft becomes robbery when in order to commit theft, or in committing theft, or in carrying away or attempting to carry away property obtained by theft, the offender voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death, hurt, or wrongful restraint. The use of force or fear of immediate harm is what elevates theft to robbery.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(22,'BNS 311','Dacoity','IPC 391','Offences Against Property','When five or more persons conjointly commit or attempt to commit a robbery, or where the whole number of persons conjointly committing or attempting to commit a robbery, and persons present and aiding such commission or attempt, amount to five or more - every person so committing, attempting, or aiding is said to commit \"dacoity\". The collective nature of the crime aggravates the offence.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine, or Life Imprisonment',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(23,'BNS 312','Dacoity with Murder','IPC 396','Offences Against Property','If any one of five or more persons who are conjointly committing dacoity commits murder in so committing dacoity, every one of those persons shall be punished with death, imprisonment for life, or rigorous imprisonment for a term up to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine. Joint criminal liability extends to all dacoits even if only one member killed.','Death, or Life Imprisonment, or Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(24,'BNS 316','Dishonest Misappropriation of Property','IPC 403','Offences Against Property','Whoever dishonestly misappropriates or converts to his own use any moveable property shall be punished. This section applies when the initial possession was lawful (e.g., property found, or entrusted temporarily) but the subsequent dealing with it is dishonest - converting it permanently to one\'s own benefit without the owner\'s authority.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(25,'BNS 317','Criminal Breach of Trust','IPC 405','Offences Against Property','Whoever, being in any manner entrusted with property, or with dominion over property, dishonestly misappropriates or converts to their own use that property, or dishonestly uses or disposes of that property in violation of any law prescribing the mode of dealing with such property - commits criminal breach of trust. The prior entrustment distinguishes this from ordinary theft.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(26,'BNS 318','Cheating','IPC 415','Offences of Fraud and Cheating','Whoever, by deceiving any person, fraudulently or dishonestly induces the person so deceived to deliver any property to any person, or to consent that any person shall retain any property, or intentionally induces the person so deceived to do or omit to do anything which he would not do or omit if he were not so deceived, and which act or omission causes or is likely to cause damage or harm to that person - commits cheating.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(27,'BNS 319','Cheating by Personation','IPC 416','Offences of Fraud and Cheating','A person is said to \"cheat by personation\" if he cheats by pretending to be some other person, or by knowingly substituting one person for another, or representing that he or any other person is a person other than he or such other person really is. Impersonating someone to gain financial or legal advantage falls squarely under this section.','Imprisonment up to 5 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(28,'BNS 336','Forgery','IPC 463','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever makes any false document or false electronic record or part of a document or electronic record with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person, or to support any claim or title, or to cause any person to part with property, or to enter into any express or implied contract, or with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed - commits forgery.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(29,'BNS 340','Forgery for Purpose of Cheating','IPC 468','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever commits forgery intending that the document or electronic record forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating shall be punished. This is a more serious offence than basic forgery - the specific intent to cheat makes the combined act graver and attracts a heavier penalty.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(30,'BNS 343','Using as Genuine a Forged Document','IPC 471','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever fraudulently or dishonestly uses as genuine any document or electronic record which he knows or has reason to believe to be a forged document or electronic record shall be punished in the same manner as if he had forged such document or electronic record. The use of a forged document is as culpable as its creation.','Same as punishment for forgery of that document type',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(31,'BNS 356','Defamation','IPC 499/500','Offences Against Reputation','Whoever, by words either spoken or intended to be read, or by signs or visible representations, makes or publishes any imputation concerning any person, intending to harm, or knowing or having reason to believe that such imputation will harm, the reputation of such person - is said to defame that person. Truth published for public good and fair comment on public conduct are exceptions.','Simple Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(32,'BNS 351','Criminal Intimidation','IPC 503/506','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever threatens another with any injury to his person, reputation, or property, or to the person or reputation of any one in whom that person is interested, with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do - commits criminal intimidation.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both; if threat to cause death/grievous hurt: up to 7 years',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(33,'BNS 352','Intentional Insult with Intent to Provoke Breach of Peace','IPC 504','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever intentionally insults, and thereby gives provocation to any person, intending or knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace, or to commit any other offence, shall be punished. The key element is the deliberate provocation intended to cause a breach of public peace.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(34,'BNS 111','Organised Crime','NEW','New Offences under BNS 2023','Whoever commits organised crime - meaning any continuing unlawful activity including extortion, trafficking, drug peddling, or contract killing undertaken by a person either singly or jointly as a member of an organised crime syndicate - shall be punished. This section specifically targets crime syndicates, gang networks, and underworld organisations that were not explicitly covered under the IPC.','Death or Life Imprisonment (if victim dies); otherwise 5 years to Life + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(35,'BNS 113','Terrorist Act','NEW','New Offences under BNS 2023','Whoever commits a terrorist act - meaning whoever does any act with intent to threaten or likely to threaten the unity, integrity, sovereignty, security, or economic security of India - shall be punished. This section brings terrorism-related provisions from UAPA and other special laws into the mainstream criminal code under BNS 2023, making the general criminal courts more empowered to deal with such cases.','Death or Life Imprisonment + Fine (if death caused); 5 years to Life (other cases)',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(36,'BNS 69_A','Sexual Intercourse on False Promise of Marriage','NEW','New Offences under BNS 2023','Whoever, by deceitful means or by making a promise to marry a woman without any intention of fulfilling such promise, induces her to have sexual intercourse with him commits an offence under this section. This provision specifically codifies a ground for prosecution that was previously handled under rape law after judicial interpretation, creating explicit statutory clarity.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(37,'BNS 147','Waging or Attempting to Wage War Against the Government of India','IPC 121','Offences Against the State','Whoever wages war against the Government of India, or attempts to wage such war, or abets the waging of such war, shall be punished. This is the most serious political offence in the code - reflecting the ultimate betrayal of loyalty to the nation. The section applies to both citizens and non-citizens who commit such acts on Indian soil.','Death, or Imprisonment for Life + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(38,'BNS 150','Acts Endangering Sovereignty, Unity and Integrity of India','IPC 124A','Offences Against the State','Whoever, purposely or knowingly, by words spoken or written, or by signs, or by visible representation, or by electronic communication, or by use of financial means, excites or attempts to excite secession or armed rebellion or subversive activities against India - shall be punished. BNS 150 replaced the colonial-era sedition law (IPC 124A) with a more precisely defined and targeted offence that focuses on actual threats to national integrity rather than mere criticism of the government.','Life Imprisonment + Fine, or Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(39,'BNS 189','Unlawful Assembly','IPC 141','Offences Against Public Tranquility','An assembly of five or more persons is designated \"unlawful assembly\" if the common object of the persons composing that assembly is: to overawe the government, to resist execution of law, to commit mischief, criminal trespass, or other offence, to seize property by force, or to compel any person by force to do what they are not legally bound to do. The specific intent (common object) is what makes an assembly unlawful.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(40,'BNS 191','Rioting','IPC 146','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whenever force or violence is used by an unlawful assembly or by any member thereof, in prosecution of the common object of such assembly, every member of such assembly is guilty of the offence of rioting. The use of violence, even by a single member of the unlawful assembly, makes all members liable for rioting - a principle of collective criminal responsibility.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(41,'BNS 197','Promoting Enmity Between Different Groups','IPC 153A','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever promotes or attempts to promote feelings of enmity, hatred, or ill-will between different religious, racial, language, or regional groups or castes or communities; or commits any act prejudicial to the maintenance of harmony between different religious, racial, language, or regional groups - shall be punished. Hate speech and communal propaganda are targeted by this section.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both; 5 years if at place of worship',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(42,'BNS 137','Kidnapping','IPC 359/360/361','Offences Against Human Body','Kidnapping is of two kinds: kidnapping from India and kidnapping from lawful guardianship. BNS 137 defines the general concept - any act of abducting or forcefully taking a person away from their lawful place of residence or guardian. Minor children and persons of unsound mind have special protections under the kidnapping provisions.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(43,'BNS 140','Kidnapping or Abducting for Ransom','IPC 364A','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever kidnaps or abducts any person and thereafter causes death of, or hurts, or threatens to kill or hurt, such person, or by his conduct gives rise to a reasonable apprehension that such person may be put to death or hurt, or causes grievous hurt to, or by force compels such person to do anything - with a view to compelling the government or any person to pay ransom - shall be punished.','Death, or Life Imprisonment + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(44,'BNS 229','False Evidence / Perjury','IPC 191','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, being legally bound by an oath or by an express provision of law to state the truth, or being bound by law to make a declaration upon any subject, makes any statement which is false, and which he either knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true - is said to give false evidence. Perjury strikes at the foundation of the justice system and is treated as a grave offence.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(45,'BNS 246','Counterfeiting Currency Notes or Bank Notes','IPC 489A','Offences Relating to Currency','Whoever counterfeits, or knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting any currency note or bank note, shall be punished. Counterfeiting currency is not merely a property crime - it is an economic offence that destabilises the nation\'s monetary system and is treated with equivalent severity to many violent crimes.','Life Imprisonment, or Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(46,'BNS 106','Causing Death by Negligence','IPC 304A','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever causes the death of any person by doing any rash or negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide shall be punished. If the accused is a registered medical practitioner causing death through gross negligence, they shall also not be allowed to be arrested without prior permission of a competent authority. This section is widely applied in road accident deaths and medical negligence fatalities.','Imprisonment up to 5 years (road accidents: up to 10 years) + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(47,'BNS 93','Exposure and Abandonment of Child Under 12 Years','IPC 317','Offences Against Children','Whoever, being the father or mother of a child under the age of twelve years, or having the care of such child, exposes or leaves such child in any place with the intention of wholly abandoning such child - shall be punished. This provision is specifically aimed at protecting very young children from being abandoned by their parents or guardians.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(48,'BNS 85','Husband or Relatives Subjecting Wife to Cruelty','IPC 498A','Offences Against Women','Whoever, being the husband or the relative of the husband of a woman, subjects such woman to cruelty shall be punished. \"Cruelty\" includes any wilful conduct likely to drive the woman to commit suicide or cause grave injury to her life, limb, or health (whether mental or physical), or harassment with a view to coercing her to meet any unlawful demand for property.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(49,'BNS 4','Punishments','IPC 53','General Provisions','The punishments to which offenders are liable under the provisions of BNS are: death, imprisonment for life, imprisonment (rigorous and simple), forfeiture of property, and fine. These are the five categories of punishments that all BNS sections draw upon. Rigorous imprisonment involves hard labour; simple imprisonment does not.','As specified under each relevant section',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(50,'BNS 8','Gender Neutral Provisions','General BNS','General Provisions','The BNS 2023 uses gender-neutral language more broadly than the IPC. The pronoun \"he\" as used in the BNS includes all genders. Additionally, BNS introduces specific provisions recognising non-binary contexts in several sections - a significant modernisation over the colonial IPC framework.','N/A - definitional provision',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(51,'BNS 14','Act Done by a Person Bound by Law','IPC 76','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done by a person who is, or who by reason of a mistake of fact and not by reason of a mistake of law in good faith believes himself to be, bound by law to do it. This provides protection to persons such as soldiers following lawful orders, police executing valid warrants, and others acting under the authority of law.','Complete defence - no punishment if genuinely bound by law',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(52,'BNS 15','Act of Judge When Acting Judicially','IPC 77','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done by a Judge when acting judicially in the exercise of any power which is, or which in good faith he believes to be, given to him by law. This provides absolute judicial immunity for acts done in good faith within the scope of judicial powers - a cornerstone of judicial independence.','Complete immunity - judicial acts protected',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(53,'BNS 34','Act Done in Good Faith for Person\'s Benefit Without Consent','IPC 92','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence by reason of any harm which it may cause to a person for whose benefit it is done in good faith, even without that person\'s consent, if the circumstances are such that it is impossible for that person to signify consent, or if that person is incapable of giving consent and has no guardian from whom consent can be obtained in time for the thing to be done with benefit.','Complete defence - medical emergencies covered',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(54,'BNS 38','Right of Private Defence of Body','IPC 97','Right of Private Defence','Every person has a right to defend their own body and the body of any other person against any offence affecting the human body. The right of private defence commences as soon as a reasonable apprehension of danger to the body arises from an attempt to commit the offence - and continues as long as such apprehension continues. It is not a licence to be an aggressor.','Complete defence - proportionate force justified',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(55,'BNS 45','Abetment of a Thing','IPC 107','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','A person abets the doing of a thing who: (1) instigates any person to do that thing; (2) engages with one or more other person or persons in any conspiracy for the doing of that thing, if an act or illegal omission takes place in pursuance of that conspiracy; or (3) intentionally aids, by any act or illegal omission, the doing of that thing. All three forms of abetment carry the same punishment as the substantive offence.','Same punishment as the principal offence abetted',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(56,'BNS 61','Criminal Conspiracy','IPC 120A/120B','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','When two or more persons agree to do, or cause to be done, (1) an illegal act, or (2) an act which is not illegal by illegal means - such an agreement is designated a \"criminal conspiracy\". A conspiracy is complete at the moment of agreement - no overt act is required for the offence to be constituted, though the punishment varies based on the nature of the agreed offence.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both; heavier if conspiracy is to commit serious crime',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(57,'BNS 177','Cheating and Dishonestly Inducing Delivery of Property','IPC 420','Offences of Fraud and Cheating','Whoever cheats and thereby dishonestly induces the person deceived to deliver any property to any person, or to make, alter, or destroy the whole or any part of a valuable security, or anything signed or sealed and capable of being converted into a valuable security, shall be punished. This is the most commonly charged form of cheating - where the deceit results in a direct property loss.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 14:18:06','2026-05-28 14:18:06'),(435,'BNS 1','Short Title, Commencement and Application','IPC 1','Preliminary','This Act may be called the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. It extends to the whole of India, and it shall come into force on such date as the Central Government may, by notification in the Official Gazette, appoint. It also applies to offences committed outside India under specific circumstances.','N/A - introductory provision',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(436,'BNS 2','Definitions','IPC 2','Preliminary','This section provides general definitions applicable throughout the Sanhita: \"act\" includes illegal omissions; \"animal\" means any living creature other than a human being; \"dishonestly\" means doing an act with the intention of causing wrongful gain or wrongful loss; \"document\" includes any electronic record; \"injury\" means any harm to body, mind, reputation or property. All definitions are to be interpreted as per this section.','N/A - definitional provision',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(437,'BNS 3','General Explanations','IPC 3-5','Preliminary','Punishments of offences committed within India and by Indian citizens outside India are governed by the Sanhita. When a person causes consequence in India partly through the act of another, or when an act partly in India and partly outside results in an offence, the Sanhita applies. This section confirms territorial and extra-territorial jurisdiction of BNS.','N/A - jurisdictional provision',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(438,'BNS 5','Commutation of Sentence','IPC 54-55','Punishments','The appropriate Government may commute any sentence of death or imprisonment for life to any other punishment the person convicted is liable to. A commutation of death into life imprisonment or rigorous imprisonment into simple imprisonment can be ordered. This power rests with the executive arm of the state.','As applicable to the commuted sentence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(439,'BNS 6','Fractions of Terms of Punishment','IPC 57','Punishments','In calculating fractions of terms of punishment, imprisonment for life shall be reckoned as equivalent to imprisonment for twenty years. This equivalence is used for computation when the law refers to a fraction such as half or one-fourth of the maximum term.','N/A - calculation provision',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(440,'BNS 7','Sentence May be (in Certain Cases) Wholly or Partly Rigorous or Simple','IPC 60','Punishments','In every case in which an offender is punishable with imprisonment which may be of either description, the court may direct that the person shall suffer the whole or any part of the imprisonment awarded to be rigorous or simple. The court has discretion in choosing the nature of imprisonment when both types are available as punishment.','As per court direction - rigorous or simple',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(441,'BNS 9','Amount of Fine','IPC 63','Punishments','Where no sum is expressed to which a fine may extend, the amount of fine to which the offender is liable is unlimited, but shall not be excessive. Courts are guided by the principle of proportionality in imposing fines. If a fixed fine is prescribed, it cannot exceed that maximum. If no maximum is stated, judicial discretion operates within bounds of reasonableness.','As specified per section; otherwise unlimited but not excessive',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(442,'BNS 10','Imprisonment for Non-Payment of Fine','IPC 64','Punishments','In every case of an offence punishable with imprisonment as well as fine, in which the offender is sentenced to a fine, whether with or without imprisonment, and in every case of an offence punishable with fine only, in which the offender is sentenced to a fine, it shall be competent to the court which sentenced such offender to direct that in default of payment of the fine, he shall suffer imprisonment for a certain term.','Imprisonment in default - duration as ordered by court',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(443,'BNS 11','Limit of Imprisonment for Non-Payment of Fine','IPC 65','Punishments','The term for which the court directs the offender to be imprisoned in default of payment of a fine shall not exceed one-fourth of the term of imprisonment which is the maximum fixed for the offence, if the offence is punishable with imprisonment as well as fine. This section sets the ceiling on default imprisonment.','Maximum 1/4 of maximum sentence for the offence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(444,'BNS 12','Fine Leviable within Six Years','IPC 70','Punishments','The fine, or any part thereof which remains unpaid, may be levied at any time within six years after the passing of the sentence, and if under the sentence the offender is liable to imprisonment for a longer period than six years, then at any time previous to the expiration of that period. Death does not discharge from liability to pay fine.','Recovery within 6 years of sentence or during imprisonment',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(445,'BNS 13','Forfeiture','IPC 61','Punishments','The punishment of forfeiture of property is available as a sentence under BNS. Courts may order forfeiture of property obtained through illegal means, forfeiture of instruments used in the commission of an offence, or forfeiture as prescribed by specific BNS provisions where property is used for criminal purposes.','Forfeiture of specified property as directed by court',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(446,'BNS 16','Act of a Child Under Seven Years','IPC 82','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done by a child under seven years of age. Absolute criminal immunity is granted to children below seven years on the ground that they are presumed incapable of forming criminal intent (doli incapax). No prosecution can be initiated against a child of this age under BNS.','Complete immunity - no offence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(447,'BNS 17','Act of a Child Above Seven but Below Twelve','IPC 83','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done by a child above seven years of age and under twelve years, who has not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge the nature and consequences of his conduct on that occasion. Immature understanding must be proved - unlike BNS 16 which gives absolute immunity, this is a conditional defence requiring evidence.','Conditional immunity - if immaturity of understanding is proved',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(448,'BNS 18','Act of a Person of Unsound Mind','IPC 84','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done by a person who, at the time of doing it, by reason of unsoundness of mind, is incapable of knowing the nature of the act, or that what he is doing is either wrong or contrary to law. The insanity defence under BNS requires total incapacity - partial unsoundness does not qualify.','Complete defence if total incapacity due to mental unsoundness is proved',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(449,'BNS 19','Act of a Person Incapable of Judgment by Reason of Intoxication','IPC 85-86','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done by a person who at the time of doing it is intoxicated - provided the intoxication was caused without his knowledge or against his will. Where intoxication was voluntary, the person is liable but the court may consider whether he was capable of forming the specific intent required for the offence. Voluntary intoxication is only a partial defence.','Full defence if involuntary; partial defence if voluntary',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(450,'BNS 20','Mistake of Fact','IPC 76-79','General Exceptions','A person is not criminally responsible for an act done by him in good faith under a mistake of fact, but not under a mistake of law. Acts done by persons bound by law, acts of soldiers executing a lawful command, acts done in pursuance of a court judgment, and acts done in good faith by persons believing they are bound by law are all covered under this cluster of general exceptions.','Complete defence - good faith mistake of fact',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(451,'BNS 21','Accident','IPC 80','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done by accident or misfortune, without any criminal intention or knowledge, in the doing of a lawful act, in a lawful manner, by lawful means, and with proper care and caution. All four elements must coexist: lawful act, lawful manner, lawful means, and due care. If any element is missing, the defence fails.','Complete defence - genuine accident without negligence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(452,'BNS 22','Act Likely to Cause Harm but Done in Good Faith','IPC 81','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence merely by reason of its being done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm, if it be done without any criminal intention to cause harm, and in good faith for the purpose of preventing or avoiding other harm to person or property. This balances the risk taken against the greater harm prevented.','Complete defence if done in good faith to prevent greater harm',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(453,'BNS 23','Communication Made in Good Faith','IPC 93','General Exceptions','No communication made in good faith is an offence by reason of any harm to the person to whom it is made, if it is made for such person\'s benefit. A doctor honestly informing a patient of a terminal diagnosis, or a lawyer candidly advising a client of a weak case, is protected under this exception even if the news causes mental distress.','Complete defence - good faith communication for benefit of recipient',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(454,'BNS 24','Act to Which a Person Consented','IPC 87-91','General Exceptions','Nothing which is not intended to cause death or grievous hurt, and which is not known to be likely to cause death, is an offence by reason of any harm it may cause to any person who has given their consent (expressly or impliedly) to suffer that harm. Consent of the injured party is a defence - but only when the harm is not death or grievous hurt.','Defence - valid only if injury is not death or grievous hurt and consent is genuine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(455,'BNS 25','Act Done in Good Faith for Benefit of Child or Person of Unsound Mind','IPC 89','General Exceptions','Nothing which is done in good faith for the benefit of a person under twelve years of age, or of unsound mind, by or by consent of the guardian or other person having lawful charge of that person, is an offence by reason of any harm which it may cause. Medical procedures on children with parental consent are protected under this provision.','Complete defence - lawful guardian consent + good faith',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(456,'BNS 26','Compulsion','IPC 94','General Exceptions','Except murder, and offences against the State punishable with death, nothing is an offence which is done by a person who is compelled to do it by threats which, at the time of doing it, reasonably cause the apprehension of instant death to that person. The threat of grievous hurt alone does not constitute compulsion - it must be a threat of instant death.','Complete defence except for murder or offences against state with death penalty',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(457,'BNS 27','Acts Causing Slight Harm','IPC 95','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence by reason that it causes, or that it was intended to cause, or that it was known to be likely to cause any harm, if that harm is so slight that no person of ordinary sense and temper would complain of such harm. This is the de minimis exception - trivial technical wrongs are not prosecutable offences.','Complete exception - trivially slight harm not prosecutable',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(458,'BNS 28','Things Done in Private Defence','IPC 96','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence which is done in the exercise of the right of private defence. This is the foundational provision - establishing the existence of the right. The subsequent sections define its scope, limits, and when it extends to causing death.','Complete defence - if within the limits of private defence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(459,'BNS 29','Right of Private Defence Against Acts of Unsound Mind etc.','IPC 98','General Exceptions','When an act, which would otherwise be a certain offence, is not that offence by reason of the youth, the want of maturity of understanding, the unsoundness of mind, or the intoxication of the person doing that act, or by reason of any misconception on the part of that person - every person has the same right of private defence against that act which he would have if the act were that offence.','Right exists equally against acts by mentally incapable persons',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(460,'BNS 30','Acts Against Which There is No Right of Private Defence','IPC 99','General Exceptions','There is no right of private defence against an act which does not reasonably cause the apprehension of death or grievous hurt, if done by a public servant acting in good faith, or by the direction of a public servant. No right exists against public servants acting within legal authority. The right is also absent where recourse to public authority is available and time permits.','No right against lawfully acting public servants or when public authority is accessible',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(461,'BNS 31','Extent to Which the Right May Be Exercised','IPC 100-106','General Exceptions','The right of private defence of body extends to voluntary causing of any harm other than death - but extends to causing death when the assault is one that causes reasonable apprehension of death, grievous hurt, rape, kidnapping, or acid attack. The right of private defence of property extends to causing death only in specified extreme circumstances such as robbery, dacoity, or arson. The right is never a licence to use more force than is necessary.','Force proportionate to threat; death justified only in extreme cases',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(462,'BNS 32','Right of Private Defence Against Deadly Assault','IPC 100','General Exceptions','The right of private defence of the body extends to the voluntary causing of death or any other harm to the assailant, if the offence which occasions the exercise of the right is one which reasonably causes apprehension that death will otherwise be the consequence of such assault; or the assault is of such a nature as to reasonably cause the apprehension of grievous hurt.','Right to cause death - only if assault causes reasonable apprehension of death or grievous hurt',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(463,'BNS 33','Special Right of Private Defence Against Mortal Assault','IPC 102-103','General Exceptions','The right of private defence of the body commences as soon as a reasonable apprehension of danger to the body arises from an attempt or threat to commit the offence, though the offence may not have been committed; and it continues as long as such apprehension of danger to the body continues. A similar principle applies for property - the right begins on apprehension and ends when it passes.','Right begins at apprehension of danger; ends when apprehension ceases',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(464,'BNS 35','Acts Done Without Criminal Intention in Good Faith','IPC 92','General Exceptions','Nothing is an offence by reason of any harm which it may cause to a person for whose benefit it is done in good faith, even without that person\'s consent, if the circumstances are such that it is impossible for that person to signify consent, or if that person is incapable of giving consent and has no guardian or other person in lawful charge from whom consent can be obtained in time for the thing to be done with benefit.','Complete defence - good faith benefit even without consent',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(465,'BNS 36','Act Causing Slight Harm - Extended Provision','IPC 95','General Exceptions','Extending the concept in BNS 27, this section confirms that nothing is an offence where it was intended or known to be likely to cause harm so slight that a person of ordinary sense and temper would not complain. This is a practical safeguard against vexatious prosecutions for trivial wrongs.','N/A - no punishment; act is not an offence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(466,'BNS 37','Acts Necessary for the Prevention of Greater Harm','IPC 81','General Exceptions','The necessity defence permits a person to cause harm in order to prevent greater harm. Where there is a conflict of competing harms and the accused chooses the lesser one in good faith, they are protected. The harm chosen must be unavoidably necessary, proportionate, and lesser than the harm avoided.','Complete defence - lesser harm chosen to prevent greater harm in good faith',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(467,'BNS 39','Right of Private Defence of Property','IPC 97','Right of Private Defence','Every person has a right, subject to the restrictions in BNS 31, to defend the property, whether moveable or immoveable, of himself or of any other person, against any act which is an offence falling under the definition of theft, robbery, mischief, or criminal trespass, or which is an attempt to commit theft, robbery, mischief, or criminal trespass.','Complete defence - proportionate force to protect property',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(468,'BNS 40','Right of Private Defence of Property Extending to Death','IPC 103','Right of Private Defence','The right of private defence of property extends under certain circumstances to the voluntary causing of death or of any other harm. These circumstances are: robbery, housebreaking by night, mischief by fire on any building used as a dwelling or custody, theft/mischief/trespass accompanied by causing apprehension of death or hurt. Only in these extreme property offences may death be caused in defence.','Right to cause death - only in robbery, night housebreaking, arson, or when death/hurt apprehended',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(469,'BNS 41','Right of Private Defence - When and How Exercised','IPC 105','Right of Private Defence','The right of private defence of property commences when a reasonable apprehension of danger to the property commences. The right of private defence of property against robbery continues as long as the offender causes or attempts to cause death or hurt or wrongful restraint to any person or the fear of instant death or hurt or wrongful restraint continues. The right ends when all danger has passed.','Right commences at apprehension; ends when danger ceases',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(470,'BNS 42','Right of Private Defence Not Available Where More Harm Than Necessary','IPC 99','Right of Private Defence','The right of private defence in no case extends to the inflicting of more harm than it is necessary to inflict for the purpose of defence. This is the proportionality principle - the force used must never exceed what is reasonably necessary to meet the threat. Excessive force removes the shield of private defence.','Loss of right if excessive force used',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(471,'BNS 43','Excess in Exercise of Right of Private Defence','IPC 106','Right of Private Defence','If in the exercise of the right of private defence against an assault which reasonably causes the apprehension of death, the defender is so situated that he cannot effectually exercise that right without risk of harm to an innocent person, his right of private defence extends to the running of that risk. This provides protection for genuine defensive acts that inadvertently harm bystanders.','Extends to unavoidable risk of harm to innocent bystanders when defending against deadly assault',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(472,'BNS 44','Acts Done by Consent Under Medical or Surgical Treatment','IPC 88','General Exceptions','Nothing which is not intended to cause death is an offence by reason of any harm which it may cause, or be intended to cause, or be known to be likely to cause, to any person for whose benefit it is done in good faith, and who has given a consent, whether express or implied, to suffer that harm, or to take the risk of that harm. Medical procedures consented to by a patient are fully protected.','Complete defence - consented medical acts in good faith',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(473,'BNS 46','Abettor - Definition','IPC 108','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','A person abets an offence who abets either the commission of an offence, or the commission of an act which would be an offence, if committed by a person capable by law of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as that of the abettor. An abettor may be prosecuted even if the principal offender is not convicted.','Same punishment as the principal offender',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(474,'BNS 47','Liability of Abettor When One Act Abetted and Different Act Done','IPC 111','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','When an act is abetted and a different act is done, the abettor is liable for the act done, in the same manner and to the same extent as if he had directly abetted it - provided that the act done was a probable consequence of the abetment and was done under the influence of the instigation, or with the aid given by abetment. The probability of the outcome is the key test.','Liable for different act if it was a probable consequence of abetment',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(475,'BNS 48','Abettor Present When Offence Committed','IPC 114','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whenever any person who is absent would be liable to be punished as an abettor, is present when the act or offence for which he would be punishable in consequence of the abetment is committed, he shall be deemed to have committed such act or offence. Physical presence during the commission of the abetted act makes the abettor a principal offender.','Treated as principal offender; same punishment',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(476,'BNS 49','Abetment in India of Offences Outside India','IPC 108A','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','A person abets an offence within the meaning of this Sanhita who, in India, abets the commission of any act without and beyond India which would constitute an offence if committed in India. This provision extends India\'s jurisdiction to cover conspiracies and instigation within India targeting crimes abroad.','Same punishment as abetment of the offence within India',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(477,'BNS 50','Punishment of Abetment if Person Abetted Does Act with Different Intention','IPC 113','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','When an act is abetted with the intention on the part of the abettor of causing a particular effect, and an act for which the abettor is liable in consequence of the abetment is done with a different intention or knowledge from that of the abettor, the punishment of the abettor shall be such as would be appropriate if the act had been done with the intention or knowledge of the abettor.','Punishment as if the abettor\'s own intention carried out',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(478,'BNS 51','Liability of Abettor for Effect Caused by the Act Abetted','IPC 115-116','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever abets the commission of an offence shall, if the act abetted is committed in consequence of the abetment, and no express provision is made by this Sanhita for the punishment of such abetment, be punished with the punishment provided for the offence. If the offence requires a special mental element and the abettor lacks it, the abettor is still liable as if they had that element.','Same as punishment for the abetted offence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(479,'BNS 52','Punishment of Abetment if Offence not Committed','IPC 115','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever abets the commission of an offence shall, if the offence be not committed in consequence of the abetment, and no express provision is made by this Sanhita for the punishment of such abetment, be punished with imprisonment of any description provided for that offence, for a term which may extend to one-fourth part of the longest term provided for that offence; or with fine; or both.','Up to 1/4 of maximum sentence for the offence + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(480,'BNS 53','Punishment of Abetment Resulting in Harm','IPC 116','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever abets the commission of an offence punishable with imprisonment shall, if that offence be not committed in consequence of the abetment, and no express provision is made for the punishment of such abetment, and hurt is done to any person as the consequence of that abetment, be punished with imprisonment up to one-half of the longest term provided for the offence.','Up to 1/2 of maximum term if hurt results from uncompleted abetment',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(481,'BNS 54','Abetting Commission of Offence by the Public Generally','IPC 117','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever abets the commission of an offence by the public generally, or by any number or class of persons exceeding ten, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both. Mass instigation - inciting a crowd to commit an offence - is a distinct and separate crime under this provision.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(482,'BNS 55','Concealing Design to Commit Offence','IPC 118-119','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever, intending to facilitate or knowing it to be likely that they will thereby facilitate the commission of an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life, voluntarily conceals by any act or omission, the existence of a design to commit such offence, shall be punished. Concealing knowledge of a plot is itself an offence - failure to disclose a serious conspiracy can attract liability.','Imprisonment up to 7 years; half term if offence not committed',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(483,'BNS 56','Public Servant Concealing Design to Commit Offence','IPC 119','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever, being a public servant, intending to facilitate or knowing it to be likely that they will thereby facilitate the commission of an offence which it is their duty to prevent, voluntarily conceals the existence of a design to commit such offence, or makes false representation as to such design, shall be punished. The standard expected of public servants is higher - their duty to prevent crime makes concealment a graver wrong.','Up to 1/2 of max punishment for the offence; if offence punishable with death: up to 10 years',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(484,'BNS 57','Public Servant with Authority to Prevent an Offence who Negligently Suffers it to be Committed','IPC 217-218','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever, being a public servant, and as such charged with the framing of records or writing, frames or causes to be framed, or translates or causes to be translated, in a manner which he knows or believes to be incorrect, with intent to cause or knowing it likely to cause injury to the public or to any person, any record, or writing is punishable. Corrupt record-keeping by officials is treated as abetment of injustice.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(485,'BNS 58','Concealing Design to Commit Offence Punishable with Imprisonment','IPC 120','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever, intending to facilitate or knowing it to be likely that they will thereby facilitate the commission of an offence punishable with imprisonment, voluntarily conceals by any act or illegal omission the existence of a design to commit such offence shall, if that offence be committed, be punished with imprisonment of the description provided for the offence, for a term which may extend to one-fourth; and if the offence be not committed, to one-eighth of the longest term of such imprisonment.','Up to 1/4 term if offence committed; up to 1/8 if not committed',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(486,'BNS 59','Punishment of Criminal Conspiracy','IPC 120B','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever is a party to a criminal conspiracy to commit an offence punishable with death, imprisonment for life, or rigorous imprisonment for a term of two years or upwards, shall, where no express provision is made for the punishment of such a conspiracy, be punished in the same manner as if he had abetted such offence. For lesser conspiracies, a 6-month term or fine applies.','Same as abetment of the conspiracy offence; 6 months + Fine for minor conspiracies',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(487,'BNS 60','Attempt to Commit Offences','IPC 511','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever attempts to commit an offence punishable by the Sanhita with imprisonment for life or imprisonment, or to cause such an offence to be committed, and in such attempt does any act towards the commission of the offence, shall, where no express provision is made by the Sanhita for the punishment of such attempt, be punished with imprisonment of any description provided for the offence for a term which may extend to one-half of the imprisonment for life or, as the case may be, one-half of the longest term of imprisonment provided for that offence.','Up to 1/2 of maximum term provided for the intended offence',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(488,'BNS 62','Attempt to Commit Suicide to Compel or Restrain Exercise of Lawful Power','IPC 309','Abetment, Criminal Conspiracy and Attempt','Whoever attempts to commit suicide with the intent to compel or restrain any public servant from doing any act in the discharge of his official duty, shall be punished. This section retains a modified form of the controversial suicide attempt provision - decriminalising ordinary suicide attempts while retaining punishment only when the attempt is used as a coercive tool against public authorities.','Simple imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(489,'BNS 64','Punishment for Rape','IPC 376','Offences Against Women','Whoever commits rape shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment of not less than ten years, which may extend to imprisonment for life, and shall also be liable to fine. Aggravated rape (by police officer, public servant, armed forces, prison staff, gang rape, rape of a minor, repeat offenders) attracts the death penalty or imprisonment for life. This section sets out the full sentencing matrix for rape.','Not less than 10 years to Life + Fine; Death in aggravated cases',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(490,'BNS 65','Punishment for Rape in Certain Cases','IPC 376A-376E','Offences Against Women','Whoever commits rape on a woman under sixteen years of age shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for not less than twenty years, which may extend to imprisonment for life. Rape causing death or persistent vegetative state is punished with rigorous imprisonment not less than twenty years or life, and may extend to death. Habitual rapists shall be punished with imprisonment for life or death.','Not less than 20 years to Life or Death for rape of minor/causing death/repeat offenders',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(491,'BNS 66','Gang Rape','IPC 376D','Offences Against Women','Where a woman is raped by one or more persons constituting a group or acting in furtherance of a common intention, each of those persons shall be deemed to have committed the offence of rape regardless of whether the other persons participated in the act. Gang rape represents a collective assault on dignity - all conspirators are equally liable.','Rigorous imprisonment not less than 20 years to Life + Fine (shared among convicts)',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(492,'BNS 67','Sexual Intercourse by Husband upon His Wife During Separation','IPC 376B','Offences Against Women','Whoever has sexual intercourse with his own wife, who is living separately from him under a decree of separation or under any custom or usage, without her consent, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which shall not be less than two years but which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Not less than 2 years up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(493,'BNS 68','Sexual Intercourse by Person in Authority','IPC 376C','Offences Against Women','Whoever, being - in a position of authority or in a fiduciary relationship; a public servant; a superintendent or manager of a jail or remand home; a member of the management or staff of a hospital; or on the management or staff of an educational institution - abuses such position or fiduciary relationship to induce or seduce any woman either in custody or in premises to have sexual intercourse, shall be punished.','Rigorous imprisonment not less than 5 years up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(494,'BNS 70','Voyeurism','IPC 354C','Offences Against Women','Whoever watches, or captures the image of a woman engaging in a private act in circumstances where she would usually have the expectation of not being observed either by the perpetrator or by any other person at the behest of the perpetrator, or disseminates such image, shall be punished. Repeated offending is punished more severely. Digital distribution of intimate images is explicitly covered.','First offence: 1 to 3 years + Fine; Subsequent offences: 3 to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(495,'BNS 71','Stalking','IPC 354D','Offences Against Women','Any man who follows a woman and contacts or attempts to contact her to foster personal interaction repeatedly despite a clear indication of disinterest by such woman, or monitors the use by a woman of the internet, email, or any other form of electronic communication - commits the offence of stalking. The digital dimension of stalking is expressly recognised and punishable.','First offence: up to 3 years + Fine; Subsequent: up to 5 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(496,'BNS 72','Disrobing a Woman','IPC 354B','Offences Against Women','Any man who assaults or uses criminal force to any woman or abets such act with the intention of disrobing or compelling her to be naked, shall be punished with imprisonment of not less than three years which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Not less than 3 years up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(497,'BNS 73','Sexual Harassment','IPC 354A','Offences Against Women','A man committing any of the following acts - (i) physical contact and advances involving unwelcome and explicit sexual overtures; (ii) demand or request for sexual favours; (iii) showing pornography against the will of a woman; (iv) making sexually coloured remarks - shall be guilty of sexual harassment. Acts under (i)-(iii) are punishable up to 3 years; sexually coloured remarks up to 1 year.','3 years for sexual contact/demands/pornography; 1 year for sexual remarks',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(498,'BNS 75','Word, Gesture or Act Intended to Insult the Modesty of a Woman','IPC 509','Offences Against Women','Whoever, intending to insult the modesty of any woman, utters any word, makes any sound or gesture, or exhibits any object intending that such word or sound shall be heard, or that such gesture or object shall be seen, by such woman, or intrudes upon the privacy of such woman, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to three years, and also with fine.','Simple imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(499,'BNS 76','Assault or Use of Criminal Force to Woman with Intent to Disrobe','IPC 354B','Offences Against Women','Any man who assaults or uses criminal force to any woman or abets such act with the intention of disrobing or compelling her to be naked shall be punished with imprisonment of not less than three years which may extend to seven years, and with fine. This section specifically targets the act of forcibly undressing a woman as a distinct criminal offence.','Not less than 3 years up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(500,'BNS 77','Cruelty by Husband or His Relatives','IPC 498A','Offences Against Women','Whoever, being the husband or the relative of the husband of a woman, subjects such woman to cruelty shall be punished. \"Cruelty\" under this section means wilful conduct likely to drive the woman to commit suicide or cause grave injury to her life, limb, or mental or physical health; or harassment with a view to coercing her or any person related to her to meet any unlawful demand for property or for dowry.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(501,'BNS 78','Trafficking of Persons','IPC 370-370A','Offences Against Women','Whoever, for the purpose of exploitation, recruits, harbours, transports, provides, or obtains a person, by means of threat, force, coercion, abduction, fraud, deception, abuse of power, or inducement - including financial inducement - shall be guilty of trafficking. Exploitation includes sexual exploitation, labour exploitation, organ removal, and slavery. Enhanced penalties apply for trafficking of children and repeat offenders.','7 years to Life + Fine; Death if multiple victims or trafficking of child',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(502,'BNS 81','Importing Foreign Girl for Illicit Intercourse','IPC 366B','Offences Against Women','Whoever imports into India from any country outside India any girl under the age of twenty-one years with intent that she may be, or knowing it to be likely that she will be, forced or seduced to illicit intercourse with another person, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to ten years and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(503,'BNS 82','Enticing or Taking Away or Detaining with Criminal Intent a Married Woman','IPC 498','Offences Against Women','Whoever takes or entices away any woman who is and whom he knows or has reason to believe to be the wife of any other man, from that man, or from any person having the care of her on behalf of that man, with intent that she may have illicit intercourse with any person, or conceals or detains with that intent any such woman, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(504,'BNS 83','Marrying Again During Lifetime of Husband or Wife','IPC 494','Offences Against Women','Whoever, having a husband or wife living, marries in any case in which such marriage is void by reason of its taking place during the life of such husband or wife, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine. This is the bigamy provision - the second marriage is not only void but also criminal.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(505,'BNS 84','Marriage Ceremony Fraudulently Gone Through Without Lawful Marriage','IPC 496','Offences Against Women','Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently goes through the ceremony of being married, knowing that he is not thereby lawfully married, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine. This covers \"fake marriages\" - going through a ceremonial performance without legal validity, thereby deceiving the other party.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(506,'BNS 86','Cohabitation Caused by Man Deceitfully Inducing Belief of Lawful Marriage','IPC 493','Offences Against Women','Every man who by deceit causes any woman who is not lawfully married to him to believe that she is lawfully married to him and to cohabit or have sexual intercourse with him in that belief, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine. This addresses the harm of fraudulent cohabitation through a fake marriage.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(507,'BNS 87','Kidnapping or Abducting Woman to Compel Her Marriage','IPC 366','Offences Against Women','Whoever kidnaps or abducts any woman with intent that she may be compelled, or knowing it to be likely that she will be compelled, to marry any person against her will, or in order that she may be forced or seduced to illicit intercourse, or knowing it to be likely that she will be forced or seduced to illicit intercourse, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(508,'BNS 88','Kidnapping, Abducting or Inducing Woman to Compel Her to Marry','IPC 366A','Offences Against Women','Whoever, by any means whatsoever, induces any minor girl under the age of eighteen years to go from any place or to do any act with intent that she may be, or knowing that it is likely that she will be, forced or seduced to illicit intercourse with another person, shall be punishable with imprisonment which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(509,'BNS 89','Selling Minor for Purposes of Prostitution','IPC 372','Offences Against Women','Whoever sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of any person under the age of eighteen years with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose, or knowing it to be likely that such person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(510,'BNS 90','Buying Minor for Purposes of Prostitution','IPC 373','Offences Against Women','Whoever buys, hires, or otherwise obtains possession of any person under the age of eighteen years with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose, or knowing it to be likely that such person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(511,'BNS 91','Habitual Dealing in Slaves','IPC 371','Offences Against Women','Whoever habitually imports, exports, removes, buys, sells, traffics, or deals in slaves, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment of either description for a term not exceeding ten years, and shall also be liable to fine. This section preserves punishment for slavery-related conduct under BNS despite the formal abolition of slavery in India.','Imprisonment for Life, or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(512,'BNS 92','Unlawful Compulsory Labour','IPC 374','Offences Against Women','Whoever unlawfully compels any person to labour against the will of that person, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both. This targets forced labour imposed without legal authority - the coercion must be actual, not merely economic pressure.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(513,'BNS 94','Hiring, Employing or Engaging a Child to Commit an Offence','NEW - no direct IPC equivalent','Offences Against Children','Whoever hires, employs, or engages any child (under 18 years) to commit any offence shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to the maximum prescribed for that offence plus an additional period. This new BNS provision specifically targets adults who use children as instruments of crime - traffickers, drug lords, and gang leaders who recruit minors are squarely targeted.','Imprisonment up to max for the offence + additional term; if offence carries death: life',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(514,'BNS 95','Procuration of Minor Girl','IPC 366A','Offences Against Children','Whoever induces any minor girl under the age of eighteen years to go from any place or to do any act with intent that she may be, or knowing that it is likely that she will be, forced or seduced to illicit intercourse with another person shall be punishable with imprisonment which may extend to ten years and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(515,'BNS 96','Importation of Girl from Foreign Country','IPC 366B','Offences Against Children','Whoever imports into India from any country outside India any girl under the age of twenty-one years with intent that she may be, or knowing it to be likely that she will be, forced or seduced to illicit intercourse with another person, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(516,'BNS 97','Selling Child for Prostitution','IPC 372','Offences Against Children','Whoever sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of any person under the age of eighteen years with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person, shall be punished. The commercial exploitation of a child\'s body is treated as a most serious offence regardless of the age at which exploitation occurs.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(517,'BNS 98','Buying Child for Prostitution','IPC 373','Offences Against Children','Whoever buys, hires, or otherwise obtains possession of any person under the age of eighteen years with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse, shall be punished. Both the buyer and the seller of a child for such purposes are equally culpable.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(518,'BNS 99','Rape of a Child','IPC 376AB','Offences Against Children','Whoever commits rape on a child below the age of twelve years shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which shall not be less than twenty years, but which may extend to imprisonment for life, and shall also be liable to fine, or with death. This is the most severe punishment in the BNS provisions for sexual offences - protecting the youngest and most vulnerable victims.','Not less than 20 years to Life + Fine, or Death',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(519,'BNS 103','Abetment of Suicide of Child or Mentally Ill Person','IPC 305','Offences Against Human Body','If any person under eighteen years of age, any insane person, any delirious person, any idiot, or any person in a state of intoxication commits suicide, whoever abets the commission of such suicide shall be punished with death or imprisonment for life, or imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years, and shall also be liable to fine. Enhanced liability applies when abetting suicide of vulnerable persons.','Death or Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(520,'BNS 104','Voluntarily Causing Hurt on Provocation','IPC 334','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever voluntarily causes hurt on grave and sudden provocation, if neither the provocation is sought nor voluntarily provoked by the offender, and if the offender did not have time to cool, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to five thousand rupees, or with both. Provocation is a mitigating factor, not a complete defence.','Imprisonment up to 1 month, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(521,'BNS 107','Endangering Life or Personal Safety of Others','IPC 304A','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever causes death of any person by doing any rash or negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide, or by driving a motor vehicle in a rash or negligent manner, shall be punished. A medical practitioner who causes death through gross negligence during medical procedure shall be tried separately with prior sanction from appropriate authority. This distinguishes ordinary negligence from medical professional negligence.','Imprisonment up to 5 years; road accidents up to 10 years; medical negligence up to 2 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(522,'BNS 110','Attempt to Commit Culpable Homicide','IPC 308','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever does any act with such intention or knowledge and under such circumstances that, if he by that act caused death, he would be guilty of culpable homicide not amounting to murder, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both; and, if hurt is caused to any person by such act, shall be punished with imprisonment up to seven years, or with fine, or with both.','Up to 3 years, or Fine; if hurt caused: up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(523,'BNS 112','Petty Organised Crime','NEW','New Offences under BNS 2023','Whoever, being a member of a group or gang, commits petty organised crime - such as theft, snatching, cheating, unauthorized selling of tickets, operating illegal lotteries, or illegal selling of liquor - shall be punished. This new BNS provision brings organised street crime under a dedicated provision for the first time in Indian criminal law, targeting gangs engaged in systematic small-scale crime.','Imprisonment not less than 1 year up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(524,'BNS 114','Murder by Life-Sentence Prisoner','IPC 303','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever, being under sentence of imprisonment for life, commits murder outside of prison or within it, shall be punished with death. This provision mandates capital punishment for those who commit murder while already serving life imprisonment - reflecting the maximum deterrence needed to restrain the most serious recidivists.','Death (mandatory)',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(525,'BNS 116','Voluntarily Causing Hurt by Dangerous Weapons or Means','IPC 324','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever, except in the case provided by BNS 104, voluntarily causes hurt by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, or by means of fire or any heated substance, or by means of any poison or any corrosive substance, or by means of any explosive substance, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(526,'BNS 118','Voluntarily Causing Grievous Hurt by Dangerous Weapons or Means','IPC 326','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever, except in the case provided for in BNS 117, voluntarily causes grievous hurt by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, or by means of fire or any heated substance, or by means of any poison or any corrosive substance, or by means of any explosive substance, shall be punished.','Imprisonment for Life, or Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(527,'BNS 119','Hurt by an Act Endangering Life or Safety','IPC 337','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever causes hurt to any person by doing any act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(528,'BNS 120','Grievous Hurt by Act Endangering Life or Safety','IPC 338','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever causes grievous hurt to any person by doing any act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine which may extend to one lakh rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine up to Rs.1,00,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(529,'BNS 121','Voluntarily Causing Grievous Hurt to Extort Property','IPC 327','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever voluntarily causes hurt, for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer or from any person interested in the sufferer, any property or valuable security, or of constraining the sufferer or any person interested in such sufferer to do anything which is illegal or which may facilitate the commission of an offence, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(530,'BNS 122','Voluntarily Causing Hurt to Extort Confession','IPC 330','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever voluntarily causes hurt for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer or from any person interested in the sufferer any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct, or for the purpose of constraining the sufferer or any person interested in the sufferer to restore or to cause the restoration of any property or valuable security or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(531,'BNS 123','Voluntarily Causing Grievous Hurt to Extort Confession','IPC 331','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever voluntarily causes grievous hurt for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer or from any person interested in the sufferer any confession or any information, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(532,'BNS 125','Voluntarily Causing Hurt to Deter Public Servant from His Duty','IPC 332-333','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever voluntarily causes hurt to any person being a public servant in the discharge of his duty as such public servant, or with intent to prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both. Grievous hurt in same context: up to ten years.','Hurt: up to 3 years; Grievous Hurt: up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(533,'BNS 128','Punishment for Wrongful Confinement','IPC 342-348','Offences Against Liberty','Under the BNS, different durations of wrongful confinement attract progressively heavier penalties. Wrongful confinement for three or more days: up to two years or fine or both. For ten or more days: up to three years and fine. For the purpose of extortion: up to three years and fine. For the purpose of extorting confession: up to three years and fine. For the purpose of committing offence: up to three years and fine.','Graduated: 1 month to 3 years + Fine based on duration and purpose',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(534,'BNS 129','Assault or Criminal Force to Public Servant','IPC 352-353','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any person otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation given by that person, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to three months, or with fine which may extend to five hundred rupees, or with both. Assault or criminal force on a public servant in the discharge of his duty: up to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Simple: up to 3 months/Fine; On public servant in duty: up to 2 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(535,'BNS 130','Assault or Criminal Force to Woman','IPC 354','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any woman, intending to outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage her modesty, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which shall not be less than one year but which may extend to five years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Not less than 1 year up to 5 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(536,'BNS 131','Assault or Criminal Force in Attempt to Commit Theft','IPC 357','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any person in attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(537,'BNS 133','Assault or Criminal Force in Attempt to Wrongfully Confine','IPC 357','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any person in attempting wrongfully to confine such person, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to five thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(538,'BNS 134','Assault or Criminal Force with Intent to Outrage Modesty of Woman','IPC 354','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever assaults or uses criminal force to any woman, intending to outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage her modesty, shall be punished. This section provides enhanced protection for women from physical assault. The minimum one-year sentence reflects the serious nature of such violations of dignity.','Not less than 1 year up to 5 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(539,'BNS 135','Kidnapping from India','IPC 360','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever conveys any person beyond the limits of India without the consent of that person, or of some person legally authorised to consent on behalf of that person, is said to kidnap that person from India. International abduction - taking a person out of India against their will - is the core of this section.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(540,'BNS 136','Kidnapping from Lawful Guardianship','IPC 361','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever takes or entices any child under the age of sixteen years if a male, or under the age of eighteen years if a female, or any person of unsound mind, out of the keeping of the lawful guardian of such child or person of unsound mind, without the consent of such guardian, is said to kidnap such child or person from lawful guardianship.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(541,'BNS 138','Abduction','IPC 362','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever by force compels, or by any deceitful means induces, any person to go from any place, is said to abduct that person. Unlike kidnapping, abduction has no age limit and may apply to any person. The act may be by force or by fraud - either suffices for an abduction charge.','Varies - punished under specific abduction-related sections',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(542,'BNS 139','Kidnapping or Abducting with Intent to Murder','IPC 364','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever kidnaps or abducts any person with intent that such person may be murdered or may be so disposed of as to be put in danger of being murdered shall be punished with imprisonment for life or rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years (Rigorous) + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(543,'BNS 141','Kidnapping or Abducting in Order to Subject Person to Grievous Hurt','IPC 366','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever kidnaps or abducts any person in order that such person may be subjected to grievous hurt, slavery, or unnatural lust of any person shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(544,'BNS 142','Wrongfully Concealing or Keeping in Confinement a Kidnapped Person','IPC 368','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever, knowing that any person has been kidnapped or has been abducted, wrongfully conceals or confines such person, shall be punished in the same manner as if he had kidnapped or abducted such person with the same intention or knowledge as that with or for which he conceals or detains such person in confinement.','Same as the kidnapping or abduction offence involved',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(545,'BNS 143','Trafficking of Person','IPC 370','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever, for the purpose of exploitation, (a) recruits, (b) transports, (c) harbours, (d) transfers, or (e) receives a person, using threats of force, coercion, abduction, fraud, deception, abuse of power, or inducement, shall be guilty of the offence of trafficking. Multiple victims, repeat offending, and trafficking of minors attract maximum sentences.','7 years to Life + Fine; Death or Life if victim is child or multiple victims',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(546,'BNS 144','Exploitation of a Trafficked Person','IPC 370A','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever knowingly or having reason to believe a person to be a trafficked person, engages such person for sexual exploitation in any manner, shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which shall not be less than three years but which may extend to five years, and also with fine; if the trafficked person is a child, the term shall not be less than five years and may extend to seven years.','Adult: 3 to 5 years; Child: 5 to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(547,'BNS 145','Habitually Dealing in Slaves','IPC 371','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever habitually imports, exports, removes, buys, sells, traffics, or deals in slaves shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment of either description for a term not exceeding ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(548,'BNS 146','Unlawful Compulsory Labour','IPC 374','Offences Against Human Body','Whoever unlawfully compels any person to labour against the will of that person shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(549,'BNS 148','Assaulting Member of Legislature','IPC 121A','Offences Against the State','Whoever within or without India conspires to commit any of the offences punishable by BNS 147 or an abetment of such offences, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment of either description which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine. Conspiracy to wage war is treated almost as seriously as waging war itself.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(550,'BNS 149','Collecting Arms with Intent to Wage War','IPC 122','Offences Against the State','Whoever collects men, arms, or ammunition or otherwise prepares to wage war with the intention of either waging or being prepared to wage war against the Government of India, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or imprisonment of either description for a term not exceeding ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(551,'BNS 151','Assaulting Member of Legislature','IPC 124','Offences Against the State','Whoever assaults or wrongfully restrains, or attempts to assault or wrongfully restrain, or overawes by means of criminal force or the show of criminal force, any member of the Legislature of India, with the intention of compelling that member to exercise or refrain from exercising, in any manner, his lawful powers, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(552,'BNS 152','Act Endangering Sovereignty of India','IPC 123','Offences Against the State','Whoever knowingly suffers to be concealed, or fails to give information of the commission or intention to commit or to the presence of any person intending or prepared to wage war against the Government of India, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description which may extend to seven years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(553,'BNS 153','Abetting Mutiny or Attempting to Seduce a Soldier, Sailor or Airman','IPC 131','Offences Relating to Armed Forces','Whoever abets the commission of any mutiny by an officer, soldier, sailor, or airman in the Army, Navy, or Air Force of India, or attempts to seduce any such officer from his allegiance or his duty, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(554,'BNS 154','Abetment of Assault by Soldier, Sailor or Airman on his Superior Officer','IPC 132','Offences Relating to Armed Forces','Whoever abets an assault by an officer, soldier, sailor or airman in the Army, Navy or Air Force of India, on any superior officer in the execution of his office shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to three years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(555,'BNS 155','Abetment of Such Assault, if the Assault Committed','IPC 133','Offences Relating to Armed Forces','Whoever abets the commission of such an assault as is described in BNS 154 shall, if such assault be committed in consequence of the abetment, be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(556,'BNS 156','Abetment of Desertion of Soldier, Sailor or Airman','IPC 135','Offences Relating to Armed Forces','Whoever abets the desertion of any officer, soldier, sailor or airman in the Army, Navy or Air Force of India shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(557,'BNS 157','Harbouring Such Deserter','IPC 136','Offences Relating to Armed Forces','Whoever, except as hereinafter excepted, knowing or having reason to believe that an officer, soldier, sailor or airman in the Army, Navy or Air Force of India has deserted, harbours such officer, soldier, sailor or airman, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(558,'BNS 158','Abetment of Act of Insubordination by Soldier, Sailor or Airman','IPC 138','Offences Relating to Armed Forces','Whoever abets what he knows to be an act of insubordination by any officer, soldier, sailor or airman in the military, naval or air service of the Government of India, shall be punished, if the act abetted be not committed in consequence of the abetment, with imprisonment which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(559,'BNS 159','Bribery at Elections','IPC 171B','Offences Relating to Elections','Whoever (i) gives a gratification to any person with the object of inducing him or any other person to exercise any electoral right or of rewarding any person for having exercised any such right; or (ii) accepts either for himself or for any other person any gratification as a reward for exercising or for inducing another person to exercise any such right - commits the offence of bribery.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(560,'BNS 160','Personation at Elections','IPC 171D','Offences Relating to Elections','Whoever at an election applies for a voting paper or votes in the name of any other person, whether living or dead, or in a fictitious name, or who having already voted at an election applies at the same election for a voting paper in his own name, and whoever abets, procures, or attempts to procure the voting by any person in any such way, commits the offence of personation at an election.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(561,'BNS 161','Undue Influence at Elections','IPC 171C','Offences Relating to Elections','Whoever voluntarily interferes or attempts to interfere with the free exercise of any electoral right, commits the offence of undue influence at an election. Threatening a voter with divine displeasure or social boycott to coerce their vote is a specific example - even without physical force, psychological coercion of an elector is an offence.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(562,'BNS 162','Making False Statement in Connection with an Election','IPC 171G','Offences Relating to Elections','Whoever, with intent to affect the result of an election, makes or publishes any statement purporting to be a statement of fact which is false and which he either knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true, in relation to the personal character or conduct of any candidate, shall be punished with fine.','Fine only',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(563,'BNS 163','Illegal Payments in Connection with an Election','IPC 171H','Offences Relating to Elections','Whoever, without the general or special authority in writing of a candidate, incurs or authorises expenses on account of the holding of any public meeting, or upon any advertisement, circular or publication, or in any other way whatsoever for the purpose of promoting or procuring the election of such candidate, shall be punished with fine.','Fine only',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(564,'BNS 164','Failure to Keep Election Accounts','IPC 171I','Offences Relating to Elections','Whoever, being required by any law for the time being in force or any rule having the force of law to keep accounts of expenses incurred at or in connection with an election, fails to keep such accounts, shall be punished with fine which may extend to five hundred rupees.','Fine up to Rs.500',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(565,'BNS 172','Counterfeiting Government Stamp','IPC 255','Offences Relating to Currency','Whoever counterfeits, or knowingly performs any part of the process of counterfeiting, any stamp issued by Government for the purpose of revenue, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(566,'BNS 173','Selling Counterfeit Government Stamp','IPC 258','Offences Relating to Currency','Whoever sells, or offers for sale, any stamp which he knows or has reason to believe to be a counterfeit of any stamp issued by Government for the purpose of revenue, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(567,'BNS 174','Fraudulent Use of Government Stamp','IPC 263','Offences Relating to Currency','Whoever fraudulently uses any Government stamp which has been before used, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(568,'BNS 175','Effacing Writing from Substance Bearing Government Stamp','IPC 263A','Offences Relating to Currency','Whoever, fraudulently or without lawful excuse, erases, removes, or makes illegible the writing on any substance which has been stamped with any Government stamp, for the purpose of using that stamp for any other purpose shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(569,'BNS 187','Affray','IPC 159-160','Offences Against Public Tranquility','When two or more persons, by fighting in a public place, disturb the public peace, they are said to \"commit an affray\". Whoever commits an affray shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to one thousand rupees, or with both. The key element is a public brawl that disturbs peace.','Imprisonment up to 1 month, or Fine up to Rs.1,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(570,'BNS 188','Provocation to Break Peace','IPC 153','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever malignantly or wantonly does any act which is likely to cause the wanton provocation of any lawful authority, shall be punished. This section bridges the gap between incitement to riot and individual provocations - protecting public order from gratuitous provocations by individuals.','Imprisonment up to 1 year + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(571,'BNS 190','Being Member of Unlawful Assembly','IPC 142','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever, being aware of facts which render any assembly an unlawful assembly, intentionally joins that assembly, or continues in it, is said to be a member of an unlawful assembly. Knowledge that the assembly is unlawful and voluntary continuation in it are both required for liability.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(572,'BNS 192','Rioting Armed with a Deadly Weapon','IPC 148','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever is guilty of rioting, being armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(573,'BNS 193','Liability of Owner or Occupier of Land on Which Unlawful Assembly is Held','IPC 154','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whenever any unlawful assembly or riot takes place, the owner or occupier of the land upon which such unlawful assembly is held, or such riot is committed, and any person having or claiming an interest in such land, shall be punishable, if they knew that such offence was being or had been committed, and failed to give the earliest possible information thereof to the principal officer of the nearest police station.','Fine up to Rs.1,000',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(574,'BNS 194','Engaging in Organized Communal Violence','NEW','New Offences under BNS 2023','This new section of BNS 2023 specifically targets organized communal or sectarian violence - group violence motivated by religion, caste, ethnicity, or language. Where groups commit violence targeting specific communities, enhanced penalties apply. BNS introduces this as a distinct offence reflecting the modern reality of mob and community-targeted attacks.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine; aggravated cases up to 10 years',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(575,'BNS 195','Communal Riots and Injuries','IPC 153B','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever makes or publishes any assertion, rumour, or report, suggesting that any class of persons cannot, by reason of their being members of any religious, racial, language or regional group or caste or community, bear true faith and allegiance to the Constitution of India or the sovereignty and integrity of India, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(576,'BNS 196','Imputations, Assertions Prejudicial to National Integration','IPC 153B','Offences Against Public Tranquility','Whoever, by words either spoken or written or by signs or by visible representations or through electronic communication, makes or publishes any imputation that any class of persons cannot, by reason of their being members of any religious, racial, language or regional group or caste or community, bear true faith and allegiance to the Constitution shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(577,'BNS 198','Public Servant Framing Incorrect Document','IPC 218','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever, being a public servant, and being as such public servant, charged with the preparation of any record or other writing, frames that record or writing in a manner which he knows to be incorrect, with intent to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, loss or injury to the public or to any person, or with intent thereby to save, or knowing it likely that he will thereby save, any person from legal punishment, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(578,'BNS 199','Public Servant in Judicial Proceeding Corruptly Making Report','IPC 219','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever, being a public servant, corruptly or maliciously makes or pronounces in any stage of a judicial proceeding, any report, order, verdict, or decision which he knows to be contrary to law, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(579,'BNS 200','Commitment for Trial or Confinement by Person Having Authority Who Knows Proceedings to be Contrary to Law','IPC 220','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever, being in a position of authority, commits or causes to be committed to imprisonment any person knowing that in committing or causing such commitment he is acting contrary to law, or who detains a person in a place of custody knowing that the detention is unlawful, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(580,'BNS 201','Intentional Omission to Apprehend on Part of Public Servant Bound to Apprehend','IPC 221-222','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever, being a public servant, legally bound as such to apprehend any person or to keep that person in confinement, intentionally omits to apprehend such person or intentionally suffers such person to escape or intentionally aids such person in escaping or attempting to escape from lawful custody, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 7 years (if person held for capital offence); 3 years otherwise',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(581,'BNS 202','Resistance or Obstruction to Lawful Apprehension','IPC 224-225','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever intentionally offers any resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself or of any other person, or escapes or attempts to escape from any custody in which he is lawfully detained, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both. If the person held for a capital offence: up to seven years.','Up to 2 years; if held for capital offence: up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(582,'BNS 203','Omission to Assist Public Servant When Bound by Law','IPC 187','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever, being bound by law to render or furnish assistance to any public servant in the execution of his public duty, intentionally omits to give such assistance, shall be punished with simple imprisonment which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to five thousand rupees, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 1 month, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(583,'BNS 204','Omission to Produce Document to Public Servant','IPC 175-176','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever, being legally bound to produce or deliver up any document, fails to produce or deliver it, shall be punished with simple imprisonment which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to five hundred rupees, or with both. If the document is required before a court of justice or law enforcement, enhanced penalties apply.','Simple Imprisonment up to 1 month, or Fine up to Rs.500, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(584,'BNS 205','False Personation of Public Servant','IPC 170','Offences by Public Servants','Whoever pretends to hold any particular office as a public servant, knowing that he does not hold such office or falsely personates any other person holding such office, and in such assumed character does or attempts to do any act under colour of such office, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(585,'BNS 206','Absence of Person Required to Attend at Certain Place','IPC 172-174','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, being legally bound to appear at a certain place or before a public servant, fails to appear at the designated time, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine, or with both. If the appearance is required before a court: up to six months. Each day of default after notice is a fresh offence.','Simple Imprisonment up to 1 month/Fine; up to 6 months if court appearance required',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(586,'BNS 207','Failure to Deliver Required Document or Produce Required Thing','IPC 175','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, being legally bound to produce a document or electronic record or any thing, fails to produce it shall be punished. Simple failure to produce: up to 1 month. Failure before a court or in court: up to 6 months. Electronic records are specifically mentioned - recognising digital evidence as fully equivalent to paper documents.','Simple Imprisonment up to 1 month; up to 6 months if before court; + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(587,'BNS 208','Refusing Oath or Affirmation When Required by Public Servant to Make It','IPC 178','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever refuses to bind himself by an oath or affirmation to state the truth when required by a public servant legally competent to require such binding, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(588,'BNS 209','Refusing to Answer Public Servant Authorised to Question','IPC 179','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, being legally bound to state the truth on any subject to any public servant, refuses to answer any question demanded of him touching that subject by such public servant in the exercise of his legal powers, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(589,'BNS 210','Refusing to Sign Statement','IPC 180','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever refuses to sign any statement made by him, when required to sign that statement by a public servant legally competent to require such signature, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to three months, or with fine which may extend to five thousand rupees, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 3 months, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(590,'BNS 211','False Statement to a Public Servant','IPC 182','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever gives to any public servant any information which he knows or believes to be false, intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, such public servant to use the lawful power of such public servant to the injury or annoyance of any person, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(591,'BNS 212','Resistance to Taking of Property by Lawful Authority','IPC 183','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever offers any resistance to the taking of any property by the lawful authority of any public servant, knowing or having reason to believe that he is a public servant, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(592,'BNS 213','Obstructing Sale of Property Offered for Sale by Authority of Public Servant','IPC 184','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever intentionally obstructs any sale of property offered for sale by the authority of any public servant as such, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to five hundred rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 month, or Fine up to Rs.500, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(593,'BNS 214','Illegal Purchase or Bid for Property Offered for Sale by Authority of Public Servant','IPC 185','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, at any sale of property held by the authority of any public servant as such, purchases or bids for any property on account of any person, whether himself or any other, whom he knows to be under a legal incapacity to purchase that property at that sale, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to two hundred rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 month, or Fine up to Rs.200, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(594,'BNS 215','Obstruction of Public Servant in Discharge of Public Functions','IPC 186','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever voluntarily obstructs any public servant in the discharge of his public functions, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to three months, or with fine which may extend to two thousand five hundred rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 months, or Fine up to Rs.2,500, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(595,'BNS 216','Obstructing Public Servant in Particular Cases','IPC 188','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, knowing that, by an order promulgated by a public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate such order, he is directed to abstain from a certain act, or to take certain order with certain property in his possession or under his management, disobeys such direction, shall be punished with simple imprisonment which may extend to one month, or with fine, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 1 month + Fine; up to 6 months if harm or risk of harm results',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(596,'BNS 217','Threat of Injury to Public Servant','IPC 189','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever holds out any threat of injury to any public servant, or to any person in whom that public servant is believed to be interested, for the purpose of inducing that public servant to do any act or to forbear or delay to do any act connected with the exercise of the public functions of such public servant, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(597,'BNS 218','Threat of Injury to Induce Person to Refrain from Applying for Protection to Public Servant','IPC 190','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever holds out any threat of injury to any person for the purpose of inducing that person to refrain or desist from making a legal application for protection against any injury to any public servant legally empowered as such to give such protection, or to cause such protection to be given, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(598,'BNS 219','Destruction of Document or Electronic Record to Prevent Its Production as Evidence','IPC 201','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that any offence has been committed, causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear, with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment, or with that intention gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 7 years (if concealing capital offence); proportionally less for other offences',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(599,'BNS 220','False Information with Intent to Cause Public Servant to Use His Lawful Power to Injury','IPC 182','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever gives to any public servant any information which they know or believe to be false, intending or knowing it to be likely that such information will cause such public servant to use his lawful power to the injury or annoyance of any person, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(600,'BNS 221','Resistance or Obstruction to Lawful Apprehension','IPC 224-225A','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever intentionally offers any resistance or illegal obstruction to the lawful apprehension of himself for any offence with which he is charged or of which he has been convicted shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(601,'BNS 222','Knowingly Omitting to Arrest Offender','IPC 225B','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, in any case not provided for in BNS 201 or 221, intentionally omits to arrest a person whom he is legally bound to arrest, or intentionally suffers such person to escape from any custody in which such person is placed under his authority, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(602,'BNS 223','Escape from Confinement or Custody Negligently Suffered by Public Servant','IPC 225','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, being a public servant legally bound as such to keep in confinement any person charged with or convicted of any offence or lawfully committed to custody, negligently suffers such person to escape from confinement, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(603,'BNS 224','Aiding Escape of, Rescuing or Harbouring Such Prisoner','IPC 130','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever knowingly aids or assists any State prisoner or prisoner of war in escaping from lawful custody, or rescues or attempts to rescue any such prisoner, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or imprisonment of either description for a term not exceeding ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(604,'BNS 225','Public Servant Disobeying Law with Intent to Cause Injury','IPC 166','Contempts of Lawful Authority','Whoever, being a public servant, knowingly disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant, intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will by such disobedience cause injury to any person, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(605,'BNS 226','Making False Statement in Declaration Binding by Law','IPC 191','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever makes any false statement which is false, and which he either knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true - in any declaration or affirmation which a law or rule authorises him to make - is said to give false evidence. This covers all forms of sworn declarations beyond court testimony.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(606,'BNS 227','Fabricating False Evidence','IPC 192','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever causes any circumstance to exist, or makes any false entry in any book or record, or electronic record, or makes any document or electronic record containing a false statement, intending that such circumstance, false entry or false statement may appear in evidence in a judicial proceeding, shall be punished as for giving false evidence.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(607,'BNS 228','Punishment for False Evidence Given in Judicial Proceeding','IPC 193','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever intentionally gives false evidence in any stage of a judicial proceeding, or fabricates false evidence for the purpose of being used in any stage of a judicial proceeding, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(608,'BNS 230','Using Evidence Known to be False','IPC 196','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever corruptly uses or attempts to use as true or genuine evidence any evidence which he knows to be false or fabricated, shall be punished in the same manner as if he gave or fabricated false evidence.','Same as false evidence - up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(609,'BNS 231','Issuing or Signing a False Certificate','IPC 197','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever issues or signs any certificate required by law to be given or signed, or relating to any fact of which such certificate is by law admissible in evidence, knowing or believing that such certificate is false in any material point, shall be punished in the same manner as if he gave false evidence.','Same as false evidence - up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(610,'BNS 232','Using as True a Certificate Known to be False','IPC 198','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever corruptly uses or attempts to use any such certificate as a true certificate, knowing the same to be false in any material point, shall be punished in the same manner as if he gave false evidence.','Same as false evidence - up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(611,'BNS 233','False Statement Made in Declaration to Person Authorised to Administer Oath','IPC 199','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, in any declaration made or subscribed by him, which declaration any court of justice, or any public servant or other person, is bound or authorised by law to receive as evidence of any fact, makes any statement which is false, and which he either knows or believes to be false, or does not believe to be true, touching any point material to the object for which the declaration is made or used, shall be punished as for giving false evidence.','Same as false evidence - up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(612,'BNS 234','Using as True Such Declaration Known to be False','IPC 200','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever corruptly uses or attempts to use as true any such declaration, knowing the same to be false in any material point, shall be punished in the same manner as if he gave false evidence.','Same as false evidence - up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(613,'BNS 235','Causing Disappearance of Evidence of Offence','IPC 201','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that any offence has been committed, causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear, with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment, shall be punished. Destroying, hiding, or altering evidence after an offence to protect the wrongdoer is treated as a distinct crime.','If capital offence concealed: up to 7 years; for other offences proportionally lower + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(614,'BNS 236','Giving False Information Respecting an Offence Committed','IPC 203','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed, gives any information respecting that offence which he knows or believes to be false, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(615,'BNS 237','Screening Offender','IPC 202','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed, intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence which he is legally bound to give, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(616,'BNS 238','Obstruction of Justice - Giving False Information to Screen Offender','IPC 203-204','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed, gives any information respecting that offence which he knows or believes to be false, or destroys, conceals, or alters any document or electronic record which might be produced as evidence of the commission of such offence, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to seven years, or fine, or both.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(617,'BNS 239','Taking Gift to Help Recover Stolen Property','IPC 212-216','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, having been a party to an offence or a receivable of stolen property, takes any gift, gratification or reward, or agrees to take any gratification or reward, as a motive or reward for restoring any property to the owner thereof, or for causing the offender to be apprehended, or for causing any information to be given which may lead to the apprehension of the offender, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(618,'BNS 240','Harbouring Offender','IPC 212','Offences Against Public Justice','Whenever an offence has been committed, whoever harbours or conceals a person whom he knows or has reason to believe to be the offender, with the intention of screening him from legal punishment, shall be punished with imprisonment - if capital offence harboured: up to 5 years; for life-sentence offences: up to 3 years; for others: up to 1 year + Fine.','Up to 5 years (capital offence); up to 3 years (life sentence offence); up to 1 year (others) + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(619,'BNS 241','Taking Gift to Screen Offender from Punishment','IPC 214','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever accepts or agrees to accept any gratification for himself or any other person, or offers or agrees to offer any gratification to any person, as a motive or reward for concealing an offence, or screening any person from legal punishment for any offence, or for not proceeding against any person for any offence, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(620,'BNS 242','Receiving Stolen Property','IPC 213','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever receives any property knowing the same to have been transferred by the commission of an offence, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(621,'BNS 243','Habitually Dealing in Stolen Property','IPC 215','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever habitually receives or deals in property which he knows or has reason to believe to have been obtained by the commission of offences shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(622,'BNS 244','Assisting in Concealment of Stolen Property','IPC 216','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever, knowing or having reason to believe that any property has been stolen or obtained in a manner constituting a theft, dishonestly receives or retains such property, or voluntarily assists in concealing or disposing of or making away with such property, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(623,'BNS 245','Fraudulently Suffering Decree for Sum Not Due','IPC 229','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever fraudulently obtains a decree or order against any person for a sum not due or for a larger sum than is due to him, or fraudulently causes a decree or order to be executed against any person after it has been satisfied, shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(624,'BNS 247','Using Government Stamp Known to be Counterfeit','IPC 489C','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever uses as genuine any currency note, bank note, or Government stamp which he knows to be forged or counterfeit shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(625,'BNS 248','Selling Counterfeit Currency Note or Bank Note','IPC 489B','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever sells, or offers for sale, or buys, or receives any forged or counterfeit currency note or bank note, knowing or having reason to believe that the same is forged or counterfeit, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(626,'BNS 249','Using as Genuine a Forged or Counterfeit Currency Note or Bank Note','IPC 489D','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever knowingly performs any part of the process of making any forged or counterfeit currency note or bank note, or buys or sells or otherwise traffics in any such note, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(627,'BNS 250','Making or Possessing Instruments for Forging Currency','IPC 489E','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever makes, or performs any part of the process of making, or buys, sells or disposes of, or is in possession of any machinery, instrument or material for the purpose of being used, or knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used, for forging or counterfeiting any currency note or bank note shall be punished with imprisonment for life or imprisonment up to ten years and fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(628,'BNS 251','Abetment of False Evidence','IPC 194-195','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever gives or fabricates false evidence, intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, any person to be convicted of an offence which is capital by law of India, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life or up to 10 years (if leads to capital conviction); same as offence if no conviction results + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(629,'BNS 252','Impersonation of Juror or Assessor','IPC 229A','Offences Against Public Justice','Whoever fraudulently enters his name upon any jury-list, or fraudulently personates any juror, or any person whose attendance is required by the process of a court upon jury service, or any assessor appointed by a court, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(630,'BNS 253','Negligent Act Likely to Spread Infection of Disease Dangerous to Life','IPC 269','Offences Against Public Health','Whoever unlawfully or negligently does any act which is, and which he knows or has reason to believe to be, likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(631,'BNS 254','Malignant Act Likely to Spread Infection of Disease Dangerous to Life','IPC 270','Offences Against Public Health','Whoever malignantly does any act which is, and which he knows or has reason to believe to be, likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(632,'BNS 255','Fouling Water of Public Spring or Reservoir','IPC 277','Offences Against Public Health','Whoever voluntarily corrupts or fouls the water of any public spring or reservoir so as to render it less fit for the purpose for which it is ordinarily used, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three months, or with fine which may extend to one thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 months, or Fine up to Rs.1,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(633,'BNS 256','Making Atmosphere Noxious to Health','IPC 278','Offences Against Public Health','Whoever voluntarily vitiates the atmosphere in any place so as to make it noxious to the health of persons in general dwelling or carrying on business in the neighbourhood or passing along a public way, shall be punished with fine which may extend to five hundred rupees.','Fine up to Rs.500',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(634,'BNS 257','Rash Driving or Riding on Public Way','IPC 279','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever drives any vehicle, or rides, on any public way in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(635,'BNS 258','Rash Navigation of Vessel','IPC 280','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever navigates any vessel in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(636,'BNS 259','Exhibition of False Light, Mark or Buoy','IPC 281','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever exhibits any false light, mark or buoy, intending or knowing it to be likely that such exhibition will mislead any navigator, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 7 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(637,'BNS 260','Conveying Person by Water for Hire in Unsafe Vessel','IPC 282','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever knowingly or negligently conveys, or causes to be conveyed, for hire any person by water in any vessel, when that vessel is in such a state or so loaded as to endanger the life of that person, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to one thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.1,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(638,'BNS 261','Causing Danger, Obstruction, or Injury in Public Way or Line of Navigation','IPC 283','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever, by doing any act, or by omitting to take order with any property in his possession or under his charge, causes danger, obstruction or injury to any person in any public way or public line of navigation, shall be punished with fine which may extend to two hundred rupees.','Fine up to Rs.200',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(639,'BNS 262','Negligent Conduct with Respect to Poisonous Substance','IPC 284','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever does, with any poisonous substance, any act in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any person, or knowingly or negligently omits to take such order with any poisonous substance in his possession as is sufficient to guard against any probable danger to human life from such poisonous substance, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(640,'BNS 263','Negligent Conduct with Respect to Fire or Combustible Matter','IPC 285','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever does, with fire or any combustible matter, any act so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person, or knowingly or negligently omits to take such order with any fire or any combustible matter in his possession as is sufficient to guard against any probable danger to human life therefrom, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(641,'BNS 264','Negligent Conduct with Respect to Explosive Substance','IPC 286','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever does, with any explosive substance, any act so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person, or knowingly or negligently omits to take such order with any explosive substance in his possession as is sufficient to guard against any probable danger to human life from that substance, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(642,'BNS 265','Negligent Conduct with Respect to Machinery','IPC 287','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever does, with any machinery, any act so rash or negligent as to endanger human life or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person, or knowingly or negligently omits to take such order with any machinery in his possession or under his care as is sufficient to guard against any probable danger to human life from such machinery, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(643,'BNS 266','Negligent Conduct with Respect to Pulling Down or Repairing Buildings','IPC 288','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever, in pulling down or repairing any building, knowingly or negligently omits to take such order with that building as is sufficient to guard against any probable danger to human life from the fall of that building or any part thereof, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(644,'BNS 267','Negligent Conduct with Respect to Animal','IPC 289','Offences Against Public Safety','Whoever knowingly or negligently omits to take such order with any animal in his possession as is sufficient to guard against any probable danger to human life, or any probable danger of grievous hurt from such animal, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine which may extend to ten thousand rupees, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine up to Rs.10,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(645,'BNS 268','Punishment for Public Nuisance','IPC 290','Offences Against Public Morals','Whoever commits a public nuisance in any case not otherwise punishable by this Sanhita, shall be punished with fine which may extend to one thousand rupees.','Fine up to Rs.1,000',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(646,'BNS 269','Continuance of Nuisance After Injunction to Discontinue','IPC 291','Offences Against Public Morals','Whoever repeats or continues a public nuisance, having been enjoined by any public servant who has lawful authority to issue such injunction not to repeat or continue such nuisance, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(647,'BNS 270','Sale of Noxious Food or Drink','IPC 272-274','Offences Against Public Health','Whoever adulterates any article of food or drink so as to make such article noxious as food or drink, intending to sell such article or knowing it to be likely that the same will be sold, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(648,'BNS 271','Adulteration of Drugs','IPC 275-276','Offences Against Public Health','Whoever adulterates any drug or medical preparation in such a manner as to lessen the efficacy or change the operation of such drug or medical preparation, or to make it noxious, intending that it shall be sold or used for, or knowing it to be likely that it will be sold or used for, any medicinal purpose, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(649,'BNS 272','Obscene Acts and Songs','IPC 294','Offences Against Public Morals','Whoever, to the annoyance of others, does any obscene act in any public place, or sings, recites or utters any obscene song, ballad, or words, in or near any public place, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three months, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(650,'BNS 273','Injuring or Defiling Place of Worship','IPC 295','Offences Relating to Religion','Whoever destroys, damages, or defiles any place of worship, or any object held sacred by any class of persons with the intention of thereby insulting the religion of any class of persons or with the knowledge that any class of persons is likely to consider such destruction, damage, or defilement as an insult to their religion, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(651,'BNS 274','Deliberate and Malicious Acts Intended to Outrage Religious Feelings','IPC 295A','Offences Relating to Religion','Whoever, with deliberate and malicious intention of outraging the religious feelings of any class by insulting its religion or religious beliefs, commits any such act, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(652,'BNS 275','Disturbing Religious Assembly','IPC 296','Offences Relating to Religion','Whoever voluntarily causes disturbance to any assembly lawfully engaged in the performance of religious worship, or religious ceremonies, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(653,'BNS 276','Trespassing on Burial Places','IPC 297','Offences Relating to Religion','Whoever, with the intention of wounding the feelings of any person, or of insulting the religion of any person, or with the knowledge that the feelings of any person are likely to be wounded, or that the religion of any person is likely to be insulted thereby, commits any trespass in any place of worship or on any place of sepulture or any place set apart for the performance of funeral rites or as a depository for the remains of the dead, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(654,'BNS 277','Theft in Dwelling House','IPC 380','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits theft in any building, tent or vessel, which building, tent or vessel is used as a human dwelling, or used for the custody of property, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(655,'BNS 278','Theft by Clerk or Servant','IPC 381','Offences Against Property','Whoever, being a clerk or servant, or being employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant, commits theft in respect of any property in the possession of his master or employer, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(656,'BNS 279','Theft After Preparation Made for Causing Death, Hurt, or Restraint to Commit Theft','IPC 382','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits theft, having made preparation for causing death, or hurt or restraint, or fear of death, or of hurt, or of restraint, to any person, in order to the committing of such theft, or in order to the effecting of his escape after the committing of such theft, or in order to the retaining of property taken by such theft, shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(657,'BNS 280','Punishment for Robbery','IPC 392','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits robbery shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine; and, if the robbery be committed on the highway between sunset and sunrise, the imprisonment may be extended to fourteen years.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine; up to 14 years if on highway at night',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(658,'BNS 281','Attempt to Commit Robbery','IPC 393','Offences Against Property','Whoever attempts to commit robbery shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(659,'BNS 282','Voluntarily Causing Hurt in Committing Robbery','IPC 394','Offences Against Property','If any person, in committing or in attempting to commit robbery, voluntarily causes hurt, such person, and any other person jointly concerned in committing or attempting to commit such robbery, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(660,'BNS 283','Robbery or Dacoity with Attempt to Cause Death or Grievous Hurt','IPC 397','Offences Against Property','If at the time of committing robbery or dacoity, the offender uses any deadly weapon, or causes grievous hurt to any person, or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person, the imprisonment with which such offender shall be punished shall not be less than seven years.','Rigorous Imprisonment not less than 7 years',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(661,'BNS 284','Attempt to Commit Robbery or Dacoity When Armed with Deadly Weapon','IPC 398','Offences Against Property','If at the time of attempting to commit robbery or dacoity, the offender is armed with any deadly weapon, the imprisonment with which such offender shall be punished shall not be less than seven years.','Rigorous Imprisonment not less than 7 years',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(662,'BNS 285','Making Preparation to Commit Dacoity','IPC 399','Offences Against Property','Whoever makes any preparation for committing dacoity shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(663,'BNS 286','Punishment of Dacoity','IPC 395','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits dacoity shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(664,'BNS 287','Belonging to Gang of Dacoits','IPC 400','Offences Against Property','Whoever, at any time after the passing of this Act, shall belong to a gang of persons associated for the purpose of habitually committing dacoity, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(665,'BNS 288','Belonging to Gang of Thieves','IPC 401','Offences Against Property','Whoever, at any time after the passing of this Act, shall belong to any wandering or other gang of persons associated for the purpose of habitually committing theft or robbery, and not being a gang of thugs or dacoits, shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(666,'BNS 289','Assembling for Purpose of Committing Dacoity','IPC 402','Offences Against Property','Whoever, at any time after the passing of this Act, shall be one of five or more persons assembled for the purpose of committing dacoity, shall be punished with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Rigorous Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(667,'BNS 290','Punishment for Mischief','IPC 425-427','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits mischief shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both. \"Mischief\" means intentionally destroying or diminishing the value of property. Enhanced penalties apply when the damage is significant, to public utilities, or causes loss exceeding defined thresholds.','Up to 6 months, or Fine; higher if significant damage or public utility',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(668,'BNS 291','Mischief by Killing or Maiming Animal','IPC 428-429','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits mischief by killing, poisoning, maiming, or rendering useless any animal or animals of the value of fifty rupees or more shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both. For animals of significant value (elephants, camels, horses): up to five years.','Up to 2 years (minor animals); up to 5 years (elephants/horses/camels) + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(669,'BNS 292','Mischief by Injury to Works of Irrigation','IPC 430','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits mischief by doing any act which causes, or which he knows to be likely to cause, a diminution of the supply of water for agricultural purposes, or for food or drink for human beings or for animals which are property, or for cleanliness or for carrying on any manufacture, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to five years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 5 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(670,'BNS 293','Mischief by Injury to Public Road, Bridge, River or Channel','IPC 431','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits mischief by doing any act which renders or which he knows to be likely to render any public road, bridge, navigable river, or navigable channel, natural or artificial, impassable or less safe for travelling or conveying property, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to five years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 5 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(671,'BNS 294','Mischief by Injury to Vessel','IPC 432-433','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits mischief by doing any act which causes or which he knows to be likely to cause the destruction or damage of any vessel in distress, wrecked or stranded, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(672,'BNS 295','Mischief by Fire or Explosive Substance with Intent to Destroy House','IPC 435-436','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits mischief by fire or any explosive substance, intending to cause damage to any building which is ordinarily used as a place of worship, as a human dwelling, or as a place for the custody of property, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(673,'BNS 296','Mischief with Intent to Destroy or Make Unsafe a Railway, Aircraft, Ship or Vehicle','IPC 437-438','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits mischief by doing any act which he knows to be likely to cause the death of any person by making any bridge, river, road or vehicle unsafe for travel or use, shall be punished with imprisonment for life or imprisonment which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(674,'BNS 297','Punishment of Criminal Trespass','IPC 447','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits criminal trespass shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three months, or with fine which may extend to five hundred rupees, or with both. \"Criminal trespass\" means entering or remaining on property to commit an offence, or to intimidate, insult, or annoy the person in possession.','Imprisonment up to 3 months, or Fine up to Rs.500, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(675,'BNS 298','House-Trespass','IPC 448','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits house-trespass shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to five thousand rupees, or with both. \"House-trespass\" means criminal trespass into any building, tent, or vessel used as a human dwelling or as a place of worship or for custody of property.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine up to Rs.5,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(676,'BNS 299','Lurking House-Trespass or House-Breaking','IPC 453','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits lurking house-trespass or house-breaking shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, and shall also be liable to fine. \"Lurking house-trespass\" is criminal trespass with concealment of purpose; \"house-breaking\" involves forcible entry through specific means.','Imprisonment up to 2 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(677,'BNS 300','House-Breaking in Order to Commit Offence Punishable with Imprisonment','IPC 454','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits lurking house-trespass or house-breaking in order to the committing of any offence punishable with imprisonment shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, and shall also be liable to fine; and, if the offence intended to be committed is theft, the term may extend to ten years.','Up to 3 years; up to 10 years if theft intended + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(678,'BNS 301','House-Breaking by Night','IPC 456-457','Offences Against Property','Whoever commits house-breaking after sunset and before sunrise, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, and shall also be liable to fine. For house-breaking by night to commit theft or an offence punishable with imprisonment: up to fourteen years.','Up to 3 years; up to 14 years if to commit theft by night + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(679,'BNS 302','Dishonest Misappropriation of Property Possessed by Deceased Person at Time of His Death','IPC 404','Offences Against Property','Whoever dishonestly misappropriates or converts to his own use property, knowing that such property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person\'s death, and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to such possession, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(680,'BNS 305','Cheating with Knowledge that Wrongful Loss May Ensue','IPC 417','Offences Against Property','Whoever cheats shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both. This is the baseline cheating punishment section - for all forms of deception that result in delivery of property or cause another to do something that results in their harm.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(681,'BNS 306','Cheating with Death Penalty or Life Imprisonment Offences','IPC 419','Offences Against Property','Whoever cheats by personation shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to five years, or with fine, or with both. Pretending to be another person to commit a fraud is a more serious form of cheating - it abuses the identity and trust associated with a real individual.','Imprisonment up to 5 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(682,'BNS 307','Fraudulent Removal or Concealment of Property','IPC 421','Offences Against Property','Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently prevents any debt or demand due to himself or to any other person from being made available for payment of a debt or demand due from himself or from such other person, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(683,'BNS 309','Putting Person in Fear of Injury in Order to Commit Extortion','IPC 385','Offences Against Property','Whoever, in order to the committing of extortion, puts any person in fear, or attempts to put any person in fear, of any injury, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(684,'BNS 313','Receiving Property Stolen in Commission of Dacoity','IPC 412','Offences Against Property','Whoever dishonestly receives or retains any stolen property, knowing or having reason to believe the property to have been transferred by the commission of dacoity, or dishonestly receives from a person, whom he knows or has reason to believe to belong to a gang of dacoits, any property, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with rigorous imprisonment for a term which may extend to ten years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Life Imprisonment or Rigorous Imprisonment up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(685,'BNS 314','Dishonestly Receiving Stolen Property','IPC 411','Offences Against Property','Whoever dishonestly receives or retains any stolen property, knowing or having reason to believe the same to be stolen property, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(686,'BNS 315','Cheating by Personation','IPC 419','Offences Against Property','Whoever cheats by pretending to be some other person, or by knowingly substituting one person for another, or representing that he or any other person is a person other than he or such other person really is, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to five years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 5 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(687,'BNS 320','Punishment for Cheating','IPC 420','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever cheats and thereby dishonestly induces the person deceived to deliver any property to any person, or to make, alter, or destroy the whole or any part of a valuable security, or anything which is signed or sealed, and which is capable of being converted into a valuable security, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(688,'BNS 321','Fraudulent Cancellation, Destruction of Will','IPC 421-423','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever fraudulently removes, conceals, destroys, defaces, or transfers any document which is or purports to be a will of a deceased person or codicil thereof, or any document which relates to or is material to the proof of a will, with the intention of preventing, hindering, or rendering inconvenient or embarrassing the discovery of the truth, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(689,'BNS 322','Fraudulent Execution of Deed of Transfer Containing False Statement of Consideration','IPC 423','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever fraudulently executes any deed of transfer containing a false statement of consideration, or any instrument purporting to transfer or subject to any charge any property, which it does not transfer or subject to that charge, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(690,'BNS 323','Fraudulent Removal or Concealment of Property','IPC 424','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently conceals or removes any property of himself or any other person, or dishonestly or fraudulently assists in the concealing or removing of any property of any other person, or dishonestly releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(691,'BNS 324','Dishonest or Fraudulent Removal or Concealment of Property','IPC 421','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently prevents any debt or demand due to himself from being made available for payment of a debt or demand due from himself, or dishonestly or fraudulently prevents any legacy given to him from being made available for payment of his debts, or dishonestly or fraudulently conceals or removes any property of himself so as to prevent distribution among his creditors, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(692,'BNS 325','Property Mark','IPC 478-479','Offences Relating to Documents','A mark used for denoting that moveable property belongs to a particular person is called a property mark. Whoever marks any moveable property or goods or any case, package or receptacle containing moveable property or goods, or uses any case, package or receptacle having any mark thereon, in a manner reasonably calculated to cause it to be believed that the property or goods so marked, or the property or goods contained in any such case, package or receptacle so marked, belong to a person to whom they do not belong, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(693,'BNS 326','Tampering with Property Mark with Intent to Cause Injury','IPC 489','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever removes, destroys, defaces, or adds to any property mark, intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, injury to any person, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(694,'BNS 327','Making a False Mark upon any Receptacle Containing Goods','IPC 487','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever makes any false mark upon any case, package, or other receptacle containing goods, in a manner reasonably calculated to cause any public servant or any other person to believe that such receptacle contains goods which it does not contain, or that it does not contain goods which it does contain, or that the goods contained in it are of a nature or quality different from the real nature or quality thereof, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(695,'BNS 328','Making False Documents','IPC 464','Offences Relating to Documents','A person is said to make a false document or false electronic record when that person dishonestly or fraudulently makes, signs, seals, executes, or transmits a document or electronic record, or affixes any electronic signature, knowing that such document, electronic record, or signature was made by another person and without their lawful authority, or when a person alters a document or electronic record after it has been made, executed, or signed.','N/A - definitional provision; punishment under specific forgery sections',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(696,'BNS 329','Counterfeiting Device or Mark Used for Authenticating Documents','IPC 466','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever counterfeits any seal, plate, or other instrument for making an impression, intending that the same shall be used for the purpose of committing any forgery which would be punishable under BNS 328, or, with such intent, has in his possession any such seal, plate or other instrument, knowing the same to be counterfeit, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and also with fine.','Life Imprisonment or up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(697,'BNS 330','Forgery of Record of Court or of Public Register','IPC 466','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever forges a document purporting to be a record or proceeding of or in a court of justice, or a register of birth, baptism, marriage, or burial, or a register kept by a public servant as such, or a certificate or document purporting to be made by a public servant in his official capacity, or an authority to institute or defend a suit, or a power of attorney, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(698,'BNS 331','Forgery of Valuable Security, Will, etc.','IPC 467','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever forges a document which purports to be a valuable security or a will, or an authority to adopt a son, or which purports to give authority to any person to make or transfer any valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest, or dividends thereon, or to receive or deliver any money, moveable property, or valuable security, or any document purporting to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money, shall be punished.','Life Imprisonment or up to 10 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(699,'BNS 332','Forgery for Purpose of Cheating','IPC 468','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever commits forgery, intending that the document or electronic record forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 7 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(700,'BNS 333','Forgery for Purpose of Harming Reputation','IPC 469','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever commits forgery, intending that the document or electronic record forged shall harm the reputation of any party, or knowing that it is likely to be used for that purpose, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, and shall also be liable to fine.','Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(701,'BNS 334','Fraudulently Using a False Instrument for Weighing','IPC 264','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever fraudulently uses any instrument for weighing which he knows to be false shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(702,'BNS 335','Fraudulently Using False Weight or Measure','IPC 265','Offences Relating to Documents','Whoever fraudulently uses any false weight or false measure of length or capacity, or fraudulently uses any weight or any measure of length or capacity as a different weight or measure from what it actually is, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(703,'BNS 337','Obscene Book or Object','IPC 292-293','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits, or in any manner puts into circulation, or for purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition, or circulation makes produces or has in his possession any obscene book, pamphlet, paper, drawing, painting, representation, or figure or any other obscene object whatsoever, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, and with fine up to two thousand rupees on first conviction.','Up to 2 years + Fine up to Rs.2,000 (first conviction); up to 5 years + Fine up to Rs.5,000 (subsequent)',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(704,'BNS 338','Sale of Obscene Objects to Young Person','IPC 293','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever sells, lets to hire, distributes, exhibits or circulates to any person under the age of twenty years any such obscene object as is referred to in BNS 337 shall be punished more severely. The law treats those who target minors with obscene material as committing a specially aggravated form of the offence.','Up to 3 years + Fine up to Rs.2,000 (first); up to 7 years + Fine up to Rs.5,000 (subsequent)',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(705,'BNS 339','Keeping Lottery Office','IPC 294A','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever keeps any office or place for the purpose of drawing any lottery not being a State lottery or a lottery authorised by the State Government, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to six months, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 6 months, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(706,'BNS 341','Criminal Intimidation','IPC 503','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever threatens another with any injury to his person, reputation, or property, or to the person or reputation of any one in whom that person is interested, with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do, as the means of avoiding the execution of such threat - shall be punished with imprisonment which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both; up to 7 years if threat is of death/grievous hurt',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(707,'BNS 342','Criminal Intimidation by Anonymous Communication','IPC 507','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever commits the offence of criminal intimidation by an anonymous communication, or having taken precaution to conceal the name or abode of the person making the threat, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years, in addition to the punishment provided for the offence by BNS 351.','Additional 2 years on top of punishment for criminal intimidation',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(708,'BNS 344','Act Caused by Inducing Person to Believe That He Will Be Rendered an Object of Divine Displeasure','IPC 508','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever voluntarily causes or attempts to cause any person to do anything which that person is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do anything which he is legally entitled to do, by inducing or attempting to induce that person to believe that he or any person in whom he is interested will become or will be rendered by some act of the offender an object of Divine displeasure if he does not do the thing which it is the object of the offender to cause him to do or omit, shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 1 year, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(709,'BNS 345','Misconduct in Public by a Drunken Person','IPC 510','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever, in a state of intoxication, appears in any public place, or in any place which it is a trespass in him to enter, and there conducts himself in such a manner as to cause annoyance to any person, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to twenty-four hours, or with fine which may extend to one thousand rupees, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 24 hours, or Fine up to Rs.1,000, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(710,'BNS 346','Defamation - Explanation of Exceptions','IPC 499','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','The ten exceptions to defamation under BNS protect: truth in public interest, fair comment on public acts of public servants, reports of proceedings of courts and Parliament, merited criticism of public interest works, censure by persons having authority, accusation made to authorised persons, imputation in good faith by authority, communication in good faith to person concerned, caution made in good faith for good of the recipient or public. None of these constitutes defamation.','N/A - exceptions to defamation liability',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(711,'BNS 347','Printing or Engraving Matter Known to be Defamatory','IPC 500','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever prints or engraves any matter, knowing or having good reason to believe that such matter is defamatory of any person, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(712,'BNS 348','Sale of Printed or Engraved Substance Containing Defamatory Matter','IPC 501','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever sells or offers for sale any printed or engraved substance containing defamatory matter, knowing that it contains such matter, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both.','Simple Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(713,'BNS 349','Words, Gestures and Acts Intended to Insult Modesty of a Woman','IPC 509','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever, intending to insult the modesty of any woman, utters any word, makes any sound or gesture, or exhibits any object, intending that such word or sound shall be heard, or that such gesture or object shall be seen, by such woman, or intrudes upon the privacy of such woman, shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to three years, and also with fine.','Simple Imprisonment up to 3 years + Fine',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(714,'BNS 350','Whoever Threatens to Make Publication','IPC 503/506','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever threatens another with any injury to his reputation, or to the reputation of any person in whom he is interested, with the intent to cause alarm or coerce that person into doing or omitting to do any act, commits criminal intimidation. The specific form involving reputation threats is covered here - blackmail threats to publish defamatory information to coerce someone are criminal intimidation.','Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both; up to 7 years if death threat',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(715,'BNS 353','Statements Conducing to Public Mischief','IPC 505','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever makes, publishes, or circulates any statement, rumour, or report with intent to cause or which is likely to cause any officer of the Army, Navy, or Air Force to mutiny or disregard his duty; or any section of the public to commit any offence against any class or community; or fear or alarm to the public or any section of the public; or hatred or ill-will between different religious, racial, language or regional groups shall be punished.','Imprisonment up to 3 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(716,'BNS 354','Punishment for Defamation','IPC 500','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever defames another shall be punished with simple imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine, or with both. Defamation is cognizable - meaning police can arrest without a warrant - reflecting the serious harm reputational attacks can cause. However, it remains bailable and compoundable.','Simple Imprisonment up to 2 years, or Fine, or Both',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(717,'BNS 355','Whoever Commits Criminal Intimidation by Letters or Messages','IPC 507','Criminal Intimidation and Defamation','Whoever commits the offence of criminal intimidation by means of any letter, electronic message, or anonymous communication, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to two years in addition to the punishment provided for the offence in BNS 351. Electronic threats and anonymous online intimidation are specifically and additionally punishable under this section.','Up to 2 years additional on top of criminal intimidation punishment',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(718,'BNS 357','Repeal and Savings','IPC General','Miscellaneous','The Indian Penal Code, 1860 (Act 45 of 1860) is hereby repealed. Notwithstanding such repeal, anything done or any action taken under the Indian Penal Code is saved. Pending proceedings, sentences, and punishments imposed under the IPC shall continue as if the IPC has not been repealed. BNS applies only to offences committed on or after 1st July 2024.','N/A - transitional provision',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29'),(719,'BNS 358','Application to Offences Committed Outside India','IPC 4','Miscellaneous','The provisions of this Sanhita apply also to any offence committed by any citizen of India in any place without and beyond India; and by any person on any ship or aircraft registered in India wherever it may be. The extra-territorial jurisdiction of the Indian criminal law is preserved and updated under BNS 2023, ensuring Indian citizens cannot escape liability by committing crimes abroad.','N/A - jurisdictional provision; punishment as per relevant section',1,'2026-05-28 15:33:29','2026-05-28 15:33:29');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `bns_sections` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

--
-- Table structure for table `case_timeline`
--

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `case_timeline`;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!50503 SET character_set_client = utf8mb4 */;
CREATE TABLE `case_timeline` (
  `timeline_id` int unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT COMMENT 'Surrogate primary key',
  `case_no` varchar(30) CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL COMMENT 'FK: parent case',
  `event_date` date NOT NULL COMMENT 'Date this event occurred or is scheduled',
  `event_title` varchar(200) CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL COMMENT 'Short event label, e.g. Bail Hearing',
  `event_note` text CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci COMMENT 'Detailed notes about the event',
  `client_visible` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1' COMMENT '1 = visible in client portal; 0 = advocate-only',
  `created_by` int unsigned DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'FK: advocate who added this entry',
  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT 'Record creation timestamp',
  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT 'Last modification timestamp',
  PRIMARY KEY (`timeline_id`),
  KEY `idx_timeline_case_no` (`case_no`),
  KEY `idx_timeline_event_date` (`event_date`),
  KEY `idx_timeline_case_visible` (`case_no`,`client_visible`),
  KEY `fk_timeline_advocate` (`created_by`),
  CONSTRAINT `fk_timeline_advocate` FOREIGN KEY (`created_by`) REFERENCES `advocates` (`advocate_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL,
  CONSTRAINT `fk_timeline_case` FOREIGN KEY (`case_no`) REFERENCES `cases` (`case_no`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=1242 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci COMMENT='Ordered legal event timeline for each case';
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

--
-- Dumping data for table `case_timeline`
--

LOCK TABLES `case_timeline` WRITE;
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `case_timeline` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `case_timeline` VALUES (1002,'ADV/2026/001','2026-05-24','Case Filed','FIR registered; bail application filed simultaneously.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1003,'ADV/2026/001','2026-05-24','Bail Hearing','Bail granted with surety of Rs.50,000.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1004,'ADV/2026/001','2026-05-24','Charge Framing','Charges under IPC Sec 420 and Sec 120B framed.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1005,'ADV/2026/001','2026-05-25','Prosecution Witness 1','PW-1 Constable Ramesh Yadav examined.',0,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1006,'ADV/2026/001','2026-05-25','Prosecution Witness 2','PW-2 Complainant Suresh Mehra examined.',0,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1007,'ADV/2026/001','2026-05-25','Cross-Examination PW-2','Cross of PW-2 completed. Discrepancies noted in testimony.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1008,'ADV/2026/001','2026-05-25','Arguments on Merits','Both counsels to present final arguments.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1009,'ADV/2026/002','2026-01-10','Plaint Filed','Suit for declaration of title and permanent injunction.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1010,'ADV/2026/002','2026-03-13','Summons Issued','Defendant served notice.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1011,'ADV/2026/002','2026-04-04','Written Statement Filed','Defendant filed WS denying all allegations.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1012,'ADV/2026/002','2026-04-10','Issues Framed','3 issues framed by the Court.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1013,'ADV/2026/002','2026-05-24','Plaintiff Evidence Begins','Affidavit in evidence filed.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1014,'ADV/2026/002','2026-05-26','Plaintiff Evidence (cont)','Documents to be exhibited.',1,1,'2026-05-27 16:31:44','2026-05-27 16:31:44'),(1015,'ADV/2026/003','2026-03-01','Writ Filed','Challenge t